(function(){
const D=globalThis.RA.D;
const C=(senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale)=>({senseId,domain,en,zh,structure,grammar,rationale,sourceType:'authored'});
const M=(wrong,right,reason,errorType='meaning')=>({errorType,wrong,right,reason});
const E=(w,origin)=>({origin,prefix:null,root:null,suffix:null,source:'Etymonline: https://www.etymonline.com/word/'+w.toLowerCase().replaceAll(' ','-')});
const Q=(id,senseId,errorType,prompt,answer,d1,d2,explain)=>({id,senseId,type:'辨義與用法',errorType,prompt,options:[answer,d1,d2],answer,explain});
const P=(w,origin,contexts,mistakes,quiz)=>D(w,{etymology:E(w,origin),contexts,mistakes,quiz});
P('whom','From Old English hwam, the dative form of who; it remains in formal object questions and relative clauses.',[C('whom.s1','疑问宾语','Whom did the editor interview after the hearing?','聽證會後，編輯採訪了誰？','whom + auxiliary + subject + verb','Interrogative pronoun used as the object of a verb.','The person receives the action of interviewing.'),C('whom.s2','关系从句宾语','The engineer to whom we spoke explained the bridge design.','我們交談過的那位工程師解釋了橋梁設計。','preposition + whom; the person whom…','Relative pronoun used as the object of a preposition or clause.','Whom refers back to the engineer as the object of spoke to.')],[M('Whom did the editor interview after the hearing? The editor interviewed who as the direct object in this formal question.','Whom did the editor interview after the hearing?','In formal grammar, the object pronoun is whom; “who” is the subject form.')],[Q('whom.q1','whom.s1','grammar','Which pronoun is the formal object in “___ did the editor interview?”','Whom','Who','Whose','The person is the object of interview.'),Q('whom.q2','whom.s2','context','In “the consultant to whom I spoke,” what does whom refer to?','The consultant who received the speaking-to.','The person who did the speaking.','The consultant’s property.','After to, whom is the object referring to the consultant.'),Q('whom.q3','whom.s1','distinction','Choose the object form for a formal question.','Whom did the panel select?','Who did the panel select?','Whose did the panel select?','The selected person is the object of select.'),Q('whom.q4','whom.s2','usage','Which relative phrase is standard in formal writing?','the author to whom the letter was addressed','the author to who the letter was addressed','the author to whose the letter was addressed','The preposition to takes the object form whom.')]);
P('whopper','From whop, “a heavy blow,” plus -er; it can mean something unusually large or a very big, unbelievable lie.',[C('whopper.s1','庞然大物','The prize-winning pumpkin was a whopper, weighing more than thirty kilograms.','得獎南瓜是個龐然大物，重量超過三十公斤。','a real / absolute whopper','Noun: something unusually large in size.' ,'The pumpkin is exceptionally large.'),C('whopper.s2','弥天大谎','He told a whopper about having met the president, though he had never visited the capital.','他謊稱見過總統，儘管他從未去過首都。','tell a whopper','Noun: a very big lie that is hard to believe.' ,'The claimed meeting never happened.')],[M('The witness told a whopper when she gave a completely accurate account supported by the recording.','The witness gave an accurate account supported by the recording.','A whopper in the lie sense is a major falsehood, not a verified account.')],[Q('whopper.q1','whopper.s1','meaning','Why was the pumpkin called a whopper?','It weighed more than thirty kilograms.','It was a small seed.','It was an unbelievable excuse.','Whopper can mean something unusually large.'),Q('whopper.q2','whopper.s2','context','Why was his claim about meeting the president a whopper?','He had never even visited the capital.','The president confirmed the meeting.','The pumpkin weighed thirty kilograms.','A whopper can be a very large lie.'),Q('whopper.q3','whopper.s1','distinction','Which object could be called a whopper for its size?','A giant pumpkin winning the fair.','A tiny button lost in the grass.','A short, accurate report.','This sense refers to something unusually large.'),Q('whopper.q4','whopper.s2','word-choice','Choose the “big lie” use.','She told a whopper about winning an award she never entered.','The fisherman caught a whopper of a trout.','The baker made an unusually large loaf.','The first is an unbelievable false claim.')]);
P('whose','From Old English hwæs, the genitive form of who; it asks about ownership and introduces possessive relative clauses.',[C('whose.s1','谁的（疑问）','Whose blue umbrella was left beside the library door?','圖書館門旁留下的藍色雨傘是誰的？','whose + noun','Interrogative determiner asking which person owns something.','The speaker asks for the owner.'),C('whose.s2','关系从句所有格','The artist whose mural covers the station wall visited the school.','壁畫覆蓋車站牆面的那位藝術家參觀了學校。','the person whose + noun','Relative determiner showing that something belongs to the person or thing mentioned.','The mural belongs to or was made by the artist.')],[M('Whose blue umbrella was left by the door? It asks which person the umbrella owns.','Whose blue umbrella was left by the door? It asks who owns the umbrella.','Whose marks possession; the person owns the umbrella, not vice versa.')],[Q('whose.q1','whose.s1','meaning','What does the question “Whose umbrella is this?” ask?','Who owns the umbrella.','Who is holding the umbrella now.','Where the umbrella was made.','Whose asks about ownership.'),Q('whose.q2','whose.s2','context','In “the artist whose mural covers the wall,” what belongs to the artist?','The mural.','The station wall.','The school visit.','Whose links the mural to its creator.'),Q('whose.q3','whose.s1','grammar','Which word asks for the owner of a coat?','Whose','Whom','Why','Whose is the possessive form used to ask about ownership.'),Q('whose.q4','whose.s2','distinction','Which sentence uses whose in a relative clause?','I met the chef whose restaurant won the award.','Whose restaurant won the award?','I met whom at the restaurant.','The first clause identifies the chef through the restaurant.')]);
P('why','From Old English hwȳ, “for what reason”; it asks for a cause, links to a reason, or names a reason itself.',[C('why.s1','为什么','Why did the laboratory close early on Friday?','實驗室星期五為什麼提早關門？','why + clause','Question adverb asking for the reason for an action or fact.','The speaker asks for the cause of closing early.'),C('why.s2','……的原因','The report explains why the river changed course after the storm.','報告解釋了暴風雨後河流改道的原因。','reason why + clause','Word used after reason or a noun to introduce a cause.','The clause gives the cause of the river’s change.'),C('why.s3','理由；原因','The main why for the redesign was to make the entrance accessible.','重新設計的主要原因是讓入口更方便通行。','the why behind + decision','Noun: the reason for something.' ,'Accessibility motivated the redesign.')],[M('Why did the laboratory close early? It asks the reason, so the answer should be a person’s name rather than a cause.','Why did the laboratory close early? It asks for the cause of the early closing.','Why asks for a reason, not simply the identity of a person.')],[Q('why.q1','why.s1','meaning','What does “Why did the lab close?” ask for?','The reason it closed.','The name of its building.','The time of sunset.','Why asks for the cause of an action.'),Q('why.q2','why.s2','context','What follows “the report explains why…”?','A clause giving the river’s reason for changing course.','A person’s possessive name.','A measurement of width.','Why introduces the cause being explained.'),Q('why.q3','why.s3','distinction','In “the why behind the redesign,” what does why mean?','The reason for the redesign.','The width of the entrance.','The method used to paint it.','As a noun, why means a reason.'),Q('why.q4','why.s1','word-choice','Choose the direct reason question.','Why did the alarm ring?','Whose alarm rang?','Whom did the alarm wake?','The first asks for the cause.')]);
P('wick','From Old English weoc, “wick”; it is the thread or strip that draws wax or oil toward a flame.',[C('wick.s1','灯芯','Trim the candle wick before lighting it so the flame stays steady.','點燃前修剪蠟燭燈芯，火焰才會穩定。','trim / light a wick','Noun: a string or strip through which melted wax or oil reaches a flame.' ,'The wick feeds fuel to the candle flame.')],[M('The candle wick carried melted wax to the flame even though the candle had no string or absorbent strip inside it.','The candle wick carried fuel to the flame through its absorbent string.','A wick is the string or strip that draws fuel toward the flame.')],[Q('wick.q1','wick.s1','meaning','Why trim the candle wick?','It helps the flame burn steadily.','It measures the candle’s width.','It blocks wax from reaching the flame.','The wick draws melted wax toward the flame.'),Q('wick.q2','wick.s1','context','What part of an oil lamp absorbs the oil?','The wick','The glass window','The metal base','Oil travels through the wick to the flame.'),Q('wick.q3','wick.s1','distinction','Which item is a wick?','The cotton strip inside a candle.','The candle’s outer wax shell.','The match used to light it.','A wick is the absorbent strip that feeds fuel.'),Q('wick.q4','wick.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate phrase.','The lamp’s wick soaked up oil before lighting.','The lamp’s wick covered the entire window.','The lamp’s wick was a metal handle.','A wick absorbs and carries fuel.')]);
P('wicked','From Middle English wicked, with earlier origin uncertain; it can mean evil, playfully naughty, or excellent in informal British speech.',[C('wicked.s1','邪恶的','The novel’s wicked ruler punished anyone who questioned his orders.','小說中的邪惡統治者懲罰所有質疑命令的人。','a wicked ruler / act','Adjective: morally very bad and willing to harm others.','The ruler deliberately harms people.'),C('wicked.s2','淘气的','The children played a wicked trick by hiding their father’s slippers in the garden.','孩子們把父親的拖鞋藏在花園裡，淘氣地捉弄了他。','a wicked trick / sense of humor','Adjective: playfully naughty rather than truly evil.','The prank is mischievous, not cruel.'),C('wicked.s3','极棒的（口语）','The band played a wicked set at the small club last night.','昨晚樂團在小俱樂部演出了一場超棒的表演。','wicked good / wicked + noun','Adjective, informal British: extremely good.','The audience loved the performance.')],[M('The ruler was wicked because he showed kindness to everyone and never harmed or threatened anyone.','The ruler was benevolent because he showed kindness and did not harm people.','Wicked in its moral sense means very bad or harmful.')],[Q('wicked.q1','wicked.s1','meaning','Why was the ruler called wicked?','He punished people who questioned him.','He protected everyone fairly.','His concert was excellent.','This sense means morally bad and harmful.'),Q('wicked.q2','wicked.s2','context','What kind of trick did the children play?','A mischievous prank with their father’s slippers.','A cruel attack on strangers.','An excellent musical performance.','The children’s act is naughty but not truly evil.'),Q('wicked.q3','wicked.s3','distinction','What did the audience think of the band’s set?','It was extremely good.','It was morally evil.','It was a child’s prank.','Informal British wicked can mean excellent.'),Q('wicked.q4','wicked.s1','word-choice','Choose the morally evil use.','The wicked landlord knowingly left tenants without heat.','They played a wicked joke on their brother.','The band played a wicked show.','The first describes deliberate harm.')]);
P('wickedness','From wicked + -ness; it names the quality of being evil or a wicked act.',[C('wickedness.s1','邪恶；恶劣','The story explores the wickedness of a ruler who exploits the poor.','故事探討一位剝削窮人的統治者所展現的邪惡。','the wickedness of + person / system','Noun: the quality of being morally very bad or cruel.','The ruler’s conduct is cruel.'),C('wickedness.s2','恶行','The judge described the arson as a wickedness that endangered the whole town.','法官稱縱火是危及全鎮的惡行。','a wickedness; acts of wickedness','Noun: a wicked or cruel act.' ,'The arson itself is the harmful deed.')],[M('The judge called the arson wickedness even though it was an accidental spark that injured nobody or damaged nothing.','The judge called the deliberate arson a wicked act because it endangered the town.','Wickedness involves moral cruelty or a harmful deed, not an innocent accident.')],[Q('wickedness.q1','wickedness.s1','meaning','What quality does the story examine?','The ruler’s cruelty and exploitation.','His excellent musical skill.','A candle’s absorbent thread.','Wickedness can mean the quality of being morally bad.'),Q('wickedness.q2','wickedness.s2','context','What did the judge call the arson?','A harmful wicked act.','A harmless prank.','A very good performance.','This sense names a cruel or wicked deed.'),Q('wickedness.q3','wickedness.s1','distinction','Which phrase describes a quality rather than one act?','the wickedness of a corrupt regime','a wickedness committed last night','a wicked trick with slippers','The first names an enduring quality or condition.'),Q('wickedness.q4','wickedness.s2','word-choice','Choose the act sense.','The deliberate poisoning was a wickedness.','The king’s wickedness shaped the entire reign.','The ruler was wicked toward the poor.','The first names a specific harmful deed.')]);
P('wicker','From wicker, an older word for pliant twigs, with earlier origin uncertain; it names woven willow or similar material.',[C('wicker.s1','柳条编织物','They carried the picnic bread in a wicker basket lined with cloth.','他們把野餐麵包放在襯布的柳條籃裡。','a wicker basket / chair','Noun/adjective: willow or similar twigs woven into baskets and furniture.','The basket is made from woven twigs.')],[M('The wicker chair was woven from solid sheets of glass rather than willow or flexible twigs.','The wicker chair was woven from willow or similar flexible twigs.','Wicker is a woven material made from twigs, not glass sheets.')],[Q('wicker.q1','wicker.s1','meaning','What was the picnic basket made from?','Woven willow or similar twigs.','A candle wick.','A solid glass sheet.','Wicker is a woven twig material.'),Q('wicker.q2','wicker.s1','context','Which object is typically wicker?','A woven basket made of flexible branches.','A steel railway car.','A paper wall covering.','The basket uses the characteristic woven material.'),Q('wicker.q3','wicker.s1','distinction','What distinguishes wicker furniture?','It is made by weaving pliant twigs or similar strands.','It is carved from a single stone block.','It is always made from glass.','Wicker refers to the woven twig material.'),Q('wicker.q4','wicker.s1','word-choice','Choose the material use.','A wicker chair stood on the porch.','A wick burned inside the candle.','The wicked chair frightened the children.','The first uses wicker to describe woven furniture.')]);
P('wide','From Old English wīd, “broad”; it describes width, a broad range, something fully open, or a shot away from its target.',[C('wide.s1','宽的','The river is too wide to cross safely at this point.','這段河面太寬，無法安全渡過。','wide road / river / gap','Adjective: measuring a long distance from one side to the other.','The river spans a large distance.'),C('wide.s2','广泛的','The survey drew a wide response from schools across the country.','這項調查獲得全國各地學校的廣泛回應。','a wide range / audience','Adjective: including many different things or people.','Many schools responded.'),C('wide.s3','大开地','She opened the window wide to let the cool air into the room.','她把窗戶大大打開，讓涼爽空氣進入房間。','open one’s eyes / a door wide','Adverb: as far open as possible.','The window is opened fully.'),C('wide.s4','偏离目标','His first shot went wide and landed beyond the left post.','他的第一腳射門偏出，落在左門柱外。','shoot / kick wide','Adverb: away from the intended point or target.','The ball misses the goal.')],[M('The goalkeeper stretched wide across the goal, but the shot went wide and landed inside the center of the net.','The goalkeeper stretched across the goal, and the shot went wide of the net.','A shot that goes wide misses outside the target, not inside the net.')],[Q('wide.q1','wide.s1','meaning','Why was the river difficult to cross?','It measured a large distance from bank to bank.','It was fully open.','The ball missed a goal.','Wide as an adjective describes side-to-side distance.'),Q('wide.q2','wide.s2','context','What does the survey’s wide response mean?','Many different schools responded.','One narrow school replied.','The window opened fully.','Wide can describe a broad range or large group.'),Q('wide.q3','wide.s3','distinction','How did she open the window?','As far open as possible.','Only a narrow crack.','Away from a target.','Wide as an adverb can mean fully open.'),Q('wide.q4','wide.s4','word-choice','What happened to the shot?','It missed outside the left post.','It crossed the line into the goal.','It opened the window.','A shot going wide misses the target.')]);
P('widen','From wide + -en, “make or become wider.”',[C('widen.s1','变宽；扩大','The town will widen the footbridge so two wheelchairs can pass side by side.','鎮上將拓寬人行橋，讓兩張輪椅能並排通過。','widen a road / gap / range','Verb: increase the width of something or of a gap, range, or difference.','The bridge will have more side-to-side space.')],[M('The builders widened the bridge by reducing its width until it became too narrow for one person.','The builders narrowed the bridge by reducing its width.','Widen means increase width, not reduce it.')],[Q('widen.q1','widen.s1','meaning','Why will the town widen the footbridge?','To let two wheelchairs pass side by side.','To make it narrower than before.','To turn it into a window.','Widen means increase the bridge’s width.'),Q('widen.q2','widen.s1','context','What does “widen the gap” mean?','Make the distance between the sides larger.','Close the gap completely.','Make the gap invisible without changing its size.','Widen increases the width or distance.'),Q('widen.q3','widen.s1','distinction','Which action widens a road?','Adding space so more lanes can fit.','Removing a lane to make it narrower.','Painting the road a different colour.','Adding side-to-side space widens it.'),Q('widen.q4','widen.s1','grammar','Which sentence uses widen transitively?','They widened the entrance by a metre.','The entrance widened during the flood.','The width was one metre.','The first has a direct object, the entrance.')]);
P('widespread','From wide + spread; it describes something found in many places or shared by many people.',[C('widespread.s1','分布广泛','Widespread flooding closed roads in three coastal provinces.','廣泛的洪災使三個沿海省份的道路封閉。','widespread damage / illness','Adjective: existing or happening in many places.','Flooding affects a broad geographic area.'),C('widespread.s2','普遍的','There is widespread agreement that the old bridge needs repairs.','人們普遍認為這座舊橋需要維修。','widespread belief / agreement','Adjective: shared or believed by many people.','Many people hold the same view.')],[M('The flooding was widespread, but it affected only one tiny puddle and no other place.','The flooding was localized because it affected only one tiny puddle.','Widespread means present in many places, not confined to one spot.')],[Q('widespread.q1','widespread.s1','meaning','How extensive was the flooding?','It affected roads in three provinces.','It affected one tiny puddle only.','It occurred in one room.','Widespread can describe something happening in many places.'),Q('widespread.q2','widespread.s2','context','What does widespread agreement mean?','Many people share the same view.','One person disagrees with everyone.','The bridge is physically broad.','This sense means shared by many people.'),Q('widespread.q3','widespread.s1','distinction','Which problem is widespread?','A disease reported across many regions.','One broken tile in one house.','A private opinion held by one person.','The first occurs in many places.'),Q('widespread.q4','widespread.s2','word-choice','Choose the “widely held” use.','Widespread belief supports the conservation plan.','Widespread flooding covered the coastline.','The road was widened for traffic.','The first describes an opinion many people hold.')]);
P('widow','From Old English widewe, ultimately related to a word meaning “widowed”; it names a woman whose husband died or the act of causing such a loss.',[C('widow.s1','寡妇','The widow kept her husband’s letters in a wooden box beside the bed.','這名寡婦把丈夫的信保存在床邊的木盒裡。','a young / grieving widow','Noun: a woman whose husband has died and who has not married again.','Her husband is deceased and she remains unmarried.'),C('widow.s2','使丧偶','The sudden accident widowed three families in the mountain village.','突發事故使山村中的三個家庭失去了配偶。','be widowed; an accident widows someone','Verb: cause someone to lose a husband or wife through death.','The accident causes spouses to be bereaved.')],[M('The woman was a widow even though her husband was alive and they were still married.','The woman was married because her husband was alive.','A widow is a woman whose husband has died and who has not remarried.')],[Q('widow.q1','widow.s1','meaning','Whose letters did the widow keep?','Her deceased husband’s letters.','Her future employer’s notes.','A child’s school reports.','A widow’s husband has died.'),Q('widow.q2','widow.s2','context','What happened to the village families?','The accident caused some spouses to lose their partners.','The accident widened their homes.','The families received new wages.','To widow someone is to cause a spouse’s death.'),Q('widow.q3','widow.s1','distinction','Which person is a widow?','A woman whose husband died and who has not remarried.','A woman whose husband is alive and still married to her.','A woman whose wife died.','The definition specifies a woman whose husband has died.'),Q('widow.q4','widow.s2','grammar','Which sentence uses widow as a verb?','The disaster widowed two children.','She became a widow last year.','The widow visited the village.','The first uses widowed as an action causing bereavement.')]);
P('widower','From widow + -er; it names a man whose wife has died and who has not married again.',[C('widower.s1','鳏夫','The widower planted roses beside the house he had shared with his wife.','這名鰥夫在曾與妻子同住的房子旁種了玫瑰。','a young / grieving widower','Noun: a man whose wife has died and who has not married again.','His wife has died and he is not remarried.')],[M('He was a widower although his wife was alive and they were still married.','He was a married man because his wife was alive.','A widower is a man whose wife has died and who has not remarried.')],[Q('widower.q1','widower.s1','meaning','Who planted roses by the house?','A man whose wife had died.','A woman whose husband had died.','A man whose wife was alive and living there.','A widower is a man whose wife has died.'),Q('widower.q2','widower.s1','context','Which person could be called a widower?','A man who has not remarried since his wife died.','A man who is still married to his living wife.','A woman whose spouse died.','The term is specifically for a bereaved man.'),Q('widower.q3','widower.s1','distinction','How does widower differ from widow?','Widower names a man; widow names a woman.','Widower names a woman; widow names a man.','They name an unmarried child.','The gender distinction separates the two terms.'),Q('widower.q4','widower.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate use.','The widower donated his late wife’s books to the library.','The widower’s wife was alive and standing beside him.','The widower was a hospital room.','The first describes a man after his wife’s death.')]);
P('width','From wide + -th, a suffix forming a noun for the distance across something.',[C('width.s1','宽度','Measure the width of the doorway before ordering the refrigerator.','訂購冰箱前，先量一下門口的寬度。','the width of a road / opening','Noun: the distance from one side of something to the other.','The doorway must fit the appliance.'),C('width.s2','布料幅宽','The tailor bought fabric with a standard width of 140 centimetres.','裁縫買了幅寬為一百四十公分的標準布料。','fabric / cloth width','Noun: the measured distance across a piece of cloth or material.','The fabric is measured from edge to edge.')],[M('The doorway’s width was measured from floor to ceiling, which records its height rather than its width.','The doorway’s height was measured from floor to ceiling.','Width is side to side; floor-to-ceiling is height.')],[Q('width.q1','width.s1','meaning','Why measure the doorway’s width?','To check that the refrigerator can pass through.','To determine the doorway’s age.','To test the refrigerator’s temperature.','Width is the side-to-side distance.'),Q('width.q2','width.s2','context','What does 140 centimetres describe for the fabric?','Its distance across from edge to edge.','Its length from the shop to the tailor.','Its weight after washing.','Fabric width is measured across the material.'),Q('width.q3','width.s1','distinction','Which measurement is width?','The distance across a table from left edge to right edge.','The distance from the floor to the tabletop.','The table’s age.','The first is side-to-side distance.'),Q('width.q4','width.s2','word-choice','Choose the textile use.','The roll’s width determines how many curtains can be cut.','The road’s width allows two trucks to pass.','The doorway width fits the fridge.','The first concerns the breadth of a roll of fabric.')]);
P('wield','From Old English wieldan, “control or govern”; it can mean handle a weapon or use power and influence.',[C('wield.s1','挥舞；使用工具','The guard wielded a wooden staff to keep the crowd away from the gate.','守衛揮舞木杖，讓人群遠離大門。','wield a weapon / tool','Verb: hold and use a weapon or tool with control.','The staff is used deliberately to direct the crowd.'),C('wield.s2','行使权力','The committee chair wields considerable influence over the final budget.','委員會主席對最終預算有相當大的影響力。','wield power / influence / authority','Verb: have and use power or influence.','The chair’s decisions shape the budget.')],[M('The chair wielded influence by having no authority and no effect on the budget decision.','The chair lacked influence because the budget decision was made without the chair’s input.','To wield influence is to possess and use it, not to have no effect.')],[Q('wield.q1','wield.s1','meaning','What did the guard use to keep the crowd back?','A wooden staff held and controlled in the hand.','A legal will.','A paper window.','Wield can mean hold and use a weapon or tool.'),Q('wield.q2','wield.s2','context','How does the chair affect the budget?','The chair uses influence over the final decision.','The chair carries a staff at the gate.','The chair has no role in the discussion.','Wield influence means use power to affect something.'),Q('wield.q3','wield.s1','distinction','Which object can someone wield literally?','A hammer used with control.','An opinion with no action.','A committee’s budget.','A hammer is a tool that can be wielded.'),Q('wield.q4','wield.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative power use.','The director wields authority over hiring decisions.','The guard wielded a staff at the gate.','She wielded a knife to cut rope.','The first means exercising institutional authority.')]);
P('wife','From Old English wīf, “woman or wife”; the common modern sense is a married woman’s partner.',[C('wife.s1','妻子','His wife joined him at the award ceremony and thanked the organizers.','他的妻子陪他參加頒獎典禮，並向主辦方致謝。','his / her wife; husband and wife','Noun: the woman to whom someone is married.' ,'She is the person’s married partner.'),C('wife.s2','旧式婚配用法','The history described a chief taking a wife from a neighboring clan.','史書記載一位首領從鄰近部族娶了一名女子為妻。','take a wife (formal / historical)','Noun: a woman taken as a marriage partner, in older or formal use.','The phrase describes entering a marriage.')],[M('She introduced her wife, although the two had never married and were not partners.','She introduced her friend, since they were not married partners.','Wife denotes a woman’s spouse, not simply any acquaintance.')],[Q('wife.q1','wife.s1','meaning','Who joined him at the ceremony?','The woman he is married to.','A committee chair.','A person he interviewed.','Wife means a married woman’s partner.'),Q('wife.q2','wife.s2','context','What does “take a wife” mean in the historical account?','Enter marriage with a woman as a partner.','Hire a woman as a cook.','Take a picture of a woman.','The formal historical phrase refers to marriage.'),Q('wife.q3','wife.s1','distinction','Which relation makes someone a wife?','She is married to the person being discussed.','She is merely a neighbor.','She works in the same office.','Marriage defines the common sense.'),Q('wife.q4','wife.s1','word-choice','Choose the spouse use.','His wife called to say she would meet him at home.','The company hired a new wife for its board.','A wife is the distance across a doorway.','The first uses wife for a married partner.')]);
P('wild','From Old English wilde, “untamed or uncontrolled”; it describes nature, loss of control, intense excitement, or wilderness.',[C('wild.s1','野生的','Wild orchids grew along the shaded trail where no gardener tended them.','沒有園丁照料的野生蘭花沿著陰涼步道生長。','wild animal / plant / habitat','Adjective: living or growing in nature, not kept or planted by people.','The orchids grow without cultivation.'),C('wild.s2','狂暴的','The wild storm tore branches from trees and flooded the road.','狂暴的風暴扯下樹枝並淹沒道路。','wild weather / behavior','Adjective: violent, stormy, or not under control.','The storm is violent and uncontrolled.'),C('wild.s3','狂热的','The crowd went wild when the home team scored in the final minute.','主隊在最後一分鐘得分時，觀眾群情激昂。','go wild with excitement','Adjective: very excited or full of strong feeling.','The crowd reacts with intense excitement.'),C('wild.s4','荒野','They camped for a week in the wilds of northern Canada.','他們在加拿大北部的荒野露營一週。','in the wild; the wilds of + place','Noun: a natural area far from towns and farms.','The campers are in remote natural land.')],[M('The wild orchids were planted and tended daily in a greenhouse, yet the label called them wild.','The cultivated orchids were planted and tended in a greenhouse.','Wild plants grow naturally rather than being cultivated by people.')],[Q('wild.q1','wild.s1','meaning','Why were the orchids called wild?','They grew naturally without a gardener.','They were planted daily in a greenhouse.','They were very excited.','Wild can describe plants growing without cultivation.'),Q('wild.q2','wild.s2','context','What did the wild storm do?','It tore branches down and flooded a road.','It made the crowd cheer.','It grew along a trail.','Wild can describe violent uncontrolled weather.'),Q('wild.q3','wild.s3','distinction','How did the crowd react to the late goal?','They became extremely excited.','They camped in remote forest.','They carefully tended orchids.','Go wild means become intensely excited.'),Q('wild.q4','wild.s4','word-choice','Choose the wilderness noun use.','The explorers crossed the wilds beyond the settlement.','Wild orchids grew by the path.','A wild storm hit the coast.','The first names a remote natural region.')]);
P('wild animal','A compound of wild + animal, an animal living freely in nature rather than being tamed or kept by people.',[C('wild animal.s1','野生动物','A wild animal crossed the road at dusk, so the driver slowed down and gave it space.','黃昏時一隻野生動物穿過道路，駕駛因此減速並讓牠通過。','a wild animal in its habitat','Noun: an animal living in nature without being tamed or kept by humans.','The animal is free in its natural environment.')],[M('The tame pet rabbit that lived in a cage and depended on its owner was described as a wild animal.','The rabbit was a domesticated pet, not a wild animal.','An animal kept and tamed by people is not wild.')],[Q('wild animal.q1','wild animal.s1','meaning','Why did the driver slow down?','An untamed animal crossed the road.','A tame dog was sitting in the car.','A wallpaper pattern moved.','A wild animal lives freely in nature.'),Q('wild animal.q2','wild animal.s1','context','Which is a wild animal?','A fox living and hunting in a forest.','A pet cat kept indoors.','A farm chicken kept in a coop.','The fox is not tamed or kept by people.'),Q('wild animal.q3','wild animal.s1','distinction','What separates a wild animal from a domestic pet?','It lives freely in nature rather than being kept by people.','It is always larger than a pet.','It has a particular coat colour.','The distinction is whether people tame or keep it.'),Q('wild animal.q4','wild animal.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate use.','A wild animal should not be approached or fed.','A wild animal is a house-trained pet living indoors.','A wild animal is a wooden basket.','The first refers to an untamed creature.')]);
P('wild plant','A compound of wild + plant, a plant growing naturally rather than being cultivated in a garden or farm.',[C('wild plant.s1','野生植物','The botanist photographed a wild plant growing between rocks above the shoreline.','植物學家拍攝了一株生長在海岸上方岩石間的野生植物。','a wild plant species','Noun: a plant that grows on its own in nature instead of being cultivated.','The plant grew without being planted by a gardener.')],[M('The wild plant was sown in a greenhouse row and watered by a gardener every morning.','The cultivated plant was sown in a greenhouse and watered every morning.','A plant deliberately sown and tended is cultivated, not wild.')],[Q('wild plant.q1','wild plant.s1','meaning','Where did the botanist find the plant?','Growing naturally between shoreline rocks.','In a greenhouse row tended by a gardener.','Inside a wicker basket.','A wild plant grows on its own in nature.'),Q('wild plant.q2','wild plant.s1','context','Which is a wild plant?','A flower growing without cultivation on a hillside.','A tomato planted in a farm field.','A houseplant in a pot.','The flower grows naturally rather than being cultivated.'),Q('wild plant.q3','wild plant.s1','distinction','What makes a garden rose different from a wild plant?','People plant and tend the garden rose.','It grows in a natural place.','It has leaves.','Cultivation distinguishes the planted rose.'),Q('wild plant.q4','wild plant.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural-growth use.','A wild plant flowered in a crack in the cliff.','The farmer cultivated the plant in neat rows.','The gardener pruned the plant in a greenhouse.','The first grows without deliberate cultivation.')]);
P('wildcatter','From wildcat, the speculative oil well drilled where no field is known, + -er; the term can extend to risky ventures.',[C('wildcatter.s1','野猫井经营者','The wildcatter leased a remote tract and drilled for oil without a nearby proven field.','這名野貓井經營者租下偏遠地區，在附近沒有已知油田的地方鑽探石油。','an independent wildcatter','Noun: someone who prospects for oil or gas where no field is known; also a promoter of speculative schemes.','The drilling is an uncertain exploration.'),C('wildcatter.s1','投机冒险者','The columnist called the unlicensed financier a wildcatter for launching high-risk schemes.','專欄作家稱這名無牌融資者是冒險投機者，因為他推出高風險計畫。','a financial wildcatter','Noun: a person who launches speculative ventures with uncertain prospects.','The schemes are risky and unproven.')],[M('The wildcatter drilled in a proven oil field with guaranteed reserves and no uncertainty.','The wildcatter explored an unproven area where the presence of oil was uncertain.','Wildcat drilling is speculative because no field is known there.')],[Q('wildcatter.q1','wildcatter.s1','meaning','Where did the wildcatter drill?','In a remote area with no proven oil field nearby.','In a fully mapped field with guaranteed reserves.','Inside the city’s waiting room.','A wildcatter explores where oil or gas has not been established.'),Q('wildcatter.q2','wildcatter.s1','context','Why is wildcat drilling risky?','The presence of oil or gas is uncertain.','The reserves are guaranteed and already mapped.','The well is a cultivated wild plant.','The term implies speculative exploration.'),Q('wildcatter.q3','wildcatter.s1','distinction','Which investor might be called a wildcatter figuratively?','Someone launching unproven, high-risk ventures.','Someone funding only guaranteed savings accounts.','Someone who studies native plants.','The figurative sense is a speculative promoter.'),Q('wildcatter.q4','wildcatter.s1','word-choice','Choose the oil-prospecting use.','The wildcatter drilled far beyond the known field.','The financier was a wildcatter of risky schemes.','The flower grew as a wild plant.','The first is the literal oil-and-gas sense.')]);
P('wildebeest','From Afrikaans wildebeest, literally “wild beast,” via Dutch; it is another name for the gnu.',[C('wildebeest.s1','牛羚；角马','A herd of wildebeest crossed the plain during the annual migration.','每年遷徙期間，一群牛羚穿越了平原。','a herd / migration of wildebeest','Noun: a large African antelope, also called a gnu, known for mass migration.','The animals migrate together across the plains.')],[M('The wildebeest was a small fish that spent its life swimming in a coral reef.','The wildebeest was a large African antelope migrating across the grassland.','A wildebeest is an African antelope, not a fish.')],[Q('wildebeest.q1','wildebeest.s1','meaning','What crossed the plain during migration?','A herd of large African antelopes.','A school of coral-reef fish.','A flock of penguins.','Wildebeest are large antelopes, also called gnus.'),Q('wildebeest.q2','wildebeest.s1','context','Where might a wildebeest migration occur?','Across African grassland.','Through an Arctic ice tunnel.','Along a city sidewalk.','The animal is a migratory African antelope.'),Q('wildebeest.q3','wildebeest.s1','distinction','Which animal is a wildebeest?','A gnu travelling with a herd.','A fish living in a coral reef.','A willow tree beside a river.','Gnu is another name for wildebeest.'),Q('wildebeest.q4','wildebeest.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate use.','A wildebeest calf stayed close to the migrating herd.','A wildebeest grew leaves in the garden.','A wildebeest ran the windmill.','The first describes the antelope and its herd.')]);
P('wilderness','From wild + -erness, an old formation meaning wild or uncultivated land; figuratively it can mean a period outside public power.',[C('wilderness.s1','荒野','The hikers carried extra water before crossing the dry wilderness.','健行者在穿越乾燥荒野前帶了額外的水。','a remote / vast wilderness','Noun: a large area of wild land where few people live.','The region is remote and largely uninhabited.'),C('wilderness.s2','在野时期','After losing the election, the former minister spent years in the political wilderness.','輸掉選舉後，這位前部長多年處於政治失勢期。','in the political wilderness','Noun: a period when someone has no public power or role.','The politician is outside government and influence.')],[M('The hikers entered a wilderness, a crowded city center full of offices and apartment blocks.','The hikers entered a remote wilderness far from towns and farms.','A wilderness is wild land with few inhabitants, not a dense city center.')],[Q('wilderness.q1','wilderness.s1','meaning','What did the hikers prepare for?','Crossing a remote, dry area with few residents.','A crowded city commute.','A political campaign.','Wilderness is a large area of wild land.'),Q('wilderness.q2','wilderness.s2','context','What happened to the former minister after the election?','They spent time outside public power.','They immediately became head of government.','They crossed a desert on foot.','Political wilderness means a period without public role or power.'),Q('wilderness.q3','wilderness.s1','distinction','Which landscape is a wilderness?','A vast remote region far from towns.','A busy shopping district.','A cultivated flower garden.','The first is wild and sparsely inhabited.'),Q('wilderness.q4','wilderness.s2','word-choice','Choose the political sense.','The party leader remained in the wilderness for several years.','The hikers crossed a wilderness in the north.','Wildlife thrived in the wilderness.','The first describes absence of political influence.')]);
P('wildflower','From wild + flower, a flowering plant growing naturally without cultivation.',[C('wildflower.s1','野生花卉','A purple wildflower grew between the stones along the mountain trail.','一朵紫色野花生長在山徑石縫之間。','a native / seasonal wildflower','Noun: a flowering plant that grows naturally without being cultivated.','The plant grows on its own beside the trail.')],[M('The wildflower grew in neat greenhouse rows after a gardener planted and tended every seed.','The cultivated flower grew in greenhouse rows after a gardener planted and tended it.','A plant deliberately sown and tended is not growing as a wildflower.')],[Q('wildflower.q1','wildflower.s1','meaning','Where did the purple flower grow?','Naturally between stones on a mountain path.','In a carefully planted greenhouse row.','Inside a wicker basket.','A wildflower grows naturally without cultivation.'),Q('wildflower.q2','wildflower.s1','context','Which plant is a wildflower?','A bloom appearing on an untended hillside.','A rose planted and pruned in a formal garden.','A crop grown in organized farm rows.','The hillside bloom grows without cultivation.'),Q('wildflower.q3','wildflower.s1','distinction','What distinguishes a wildflower from a garden flower?','It grows naturally rather than being deliberately cultivated.','It always has purple petals.','It grows only in winter.','Cultivation, not color, distinguishes the term.'),Q('wildflower.q4','wildflower.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural-growth use.','A wildflower opened beside the forest path.','The gardener transplanted the wildflower into a greenhouse row.','The farmer harvested a planted crop.','The first describes a flower growing naturally.')]);
P('wildlife','From wild + life; it names animals and plants living freely in nature or the public concern for their study and protection.',[C('wildlife.s1','野生生物','The reserve protects wildlife including otters, herons, and native plants.','這座保護區保護水獺、蒼鷺和本地植物等野生生物。','protect / observe wildlife','Noun: animals, birds, and plants living free in nature.','The reserve protects naturally living species.'),C('wildlife.s2','野生生物保护','The town’s wildlife program funds habitat surveys and rescue work.','鎮上的野生生物計畫資助棲地調查和救援工作。','wildlife conservation / management','Noun: the care and study of wild living things as a public concern.','The program supports conservation and research.')],[M('The reserve’s wildlife included only plastic decorations and no living animals or plants.','The reserve’s wildlife included living animals and native plants.','Wildlife refers to living species, not plastic decorations.')],[Q('wildlife.q1','wildlife.s1','meaning','Which living things did the reserve protect?','Otters, herons, and native plants.','Only plastic ornaments.','Only garden tools.','Wildlife includes animals and plants living freely in nature.'),Q('wildlife.q2','wildlife.s2','context','What does the town’s wildlife program fund?','Habitat surveys and rescue work.','A window installation project.','A political campaign.','Wildlife can refer to public conservation and study.'),Q('wildlife.q3','wildlife.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses wildlife for living species?','The forest supports wildlife such as foxes and native flowers.','The office’s wildlife committee discussed conservation policy.','The wildlife law funds habitat surveys.','The first names the animals and plants themselves.'),Q('wildlife.q4','wildlife.s2','word-choice','Choose the conservation-topic use.','Wildlife management balances habitat protection and public access.','The reserve contains abundant wildlife.','A deer is part of the local wildlife.','The first refers to the care and management issue.')]);
P('wilds','From the plural of wild, used as a noun for remote natural regions.',[C('wilds.s1','荒野；边远地区','The survey team traveled deep into the wilds of northern Alaska.','調查隊深入阿拉斯加北部人煙稀少的荒野。','the wilds of + region','Plural noun: a large area of natural land far from towns, where few people live.','The team reaches a remote landscape.')],[M('They reached the wilds of the city center, surrounded by dense offices and crowded apartment towers.','They reached the remote wilds beyond the city center.','The wilds are remote natural areas, not a dense urban center.')],[Q('wilds.q1','wilds.s1','meaning','Where did the survey team travel?','A remote natural region in northern Alaska.','A crowded downtown district.','A greenhouse.','The wilds are far from towns and sparsely inhabited.'),Q('wilds.q2','wilds.s1','context','Which place could be called “the wilds”?','A distant stretch of forest beyond settled roads.','A busy shopping mall.','A city council chamber.','The phrase refers to remote natural land.'),Q('wilds.q3','wilds.s1','distinction','What contrasts with the wilds?','A densely populated city.','A remote uninhabited plain.','A vast natural forest.','The city is settled and crowded.'),Q('wilds.q4','wilds.s1','word-choice','Choose the regional noun use.','They built a research camp in the wilds of Patagonia.','They studied wild orchids in a garden.','The animal was wild and untamed.','The first uses wilds for a remote region.')]);
P('will','From Old English willan, “wish or be willing”; it is a future auxiliary, expresses willingness or insistence, and names intention, testament, or mental effort.',[C('will.s1','将来','The museum will reopen its east gallery next month.','博物館下個月將重新開放東側展廳。','will + base verb','Modal auxiliary used to talk about the future.','The reopening is planned for a future time.'),C('will.s2','愿意','I will carry the boxes upstairs if you hold the door.','如果你扶著門，我願意把箱子搬上樓。','will + base verb; be willing to','Modal auxiliary expressing readiness or agreement.','The speaker offers to help.'),C('will.s3','偏要；总是','He will leave every cupboard door open, even after being reminded.','即使有人提醒，他還是偏要把每扇櫥櫃門都敞開。','will keep / will always','Modal auxiliary for a firm order or an annoying repeated habit.','The repeated behavior frustrates others.'),C('will.s4','意志力','Her will carried her through months of rehabilitation.','她靠著堅強意志熬過數月復健。','strength / force of will','Noun: the mental power to choose and keep going.','Determination sustains her.'),C('will.s5','遗嘱','The lawyer read the will to explain who would receive the house.','律師宣讀遺囑，說明房子將由誰繼承。','make / leave / read a will','Noun: a legal document stating who receives property after death.','The document names beneficiaries.'),C('will.s6','立遗嘱；用意志促成','She willed herself to stay calm before the interview.','面試前，她努力讓自己保持冷靜。','will yourself to do something; will property to someone','Verb: try to make something happen by mental effort, or leave property by will.','She uses mental effort to remain calm.')],[M('The lawyer read the will to explain who would receive the house, but the document contained no instructions about anyone’s property.','The lawyer read the will, which stated who would receive the house.','A will is a legal document that directs how property is distributed.')],[Q('will.q1','will.s1','meaning','When will the museum reopen?','Next month.','Last month.','Only if the east gallery closes forever.','Will with a base verb can refer to the future.'),Q('will.q2','will.s2','context','What does the speaker offer to do?','Carry the boxes upstairs.','Leave every cupboard open.','Read a legal document.','Here will expresses willingness.'),Q('will.q3','will.s5','distinction','What did the lawyer read?','A legal document naming who inherits property.','A forecast about next month.','A person’s strength of character.','A will is a testament.'),Q('will.q4','will.s6','word-choice','What did she do before the interview?','Used mental effort to keep herself calm.','Signed a deed giving away her house.','Reopened the museum gallery.','Will oneself to do something is a deliberate mental effort.')]);
P('willful','From will + -ful; it means stubbornly determined to do as one wishes or deliberately intentional.',[C('willful.s1','固执任性；蓄意','The willful driver ignored the road closure and pushed past the barrier.','這名任性的駕駛無視道路封閉，硬闖過柵欄。','willful disobedience / damage','Adjective: stubbornly doing what one wants, or acting deliberately.','The driver knowingly ignores the closure.')],[M('The child’s willful damage was a complete accident that happened while the child was asleep.','The child’s damage was accidental because it happened while asleep.','Willful damage is deliberate, not an unconscious accident.')],[Q('willful.q1','willful.s1','meaning','Why was the driver described as willful?','The driver knowingly ignored the road closure.','The driver did not know a road was closed.','The driver obeyed every sign.','Willful behavior is deliberate or stubborn.'),Q('willful.q2','willful.s1','context','Which act is willful disobedience?','A student deliberately refuses a clearly stated rule.','A student misses a rule that was never explained.','A student follows the rule carefully.','The refusal is intentional.'),Q('willful.q3','willful.s1','distinction','How does willful differ from accidental?','It is done deliberately or stubbornly.','It happens without intention.','It describes something very wide.','Willful emphasizes intention.'),Q('willful.q4','willful.s1','word-choice','Choose the deliberate-damage use.','Investigators found the fire was caused by willful damage.','The fire started by accident during a storm.','The damage occurred with no human action.','The first identifies deliberate conduct.')]);
P('willing','From will + -ing; it describes readiness to act freely or an action done by choice.',[C('willing.s1','愿意的','The volunteer was willing to stay late to help close the shelter.','這名志工願意留下來，協助關閉收容所。','be willing to + verb','Adjective: ready and happy to do something without being forced.','The volunteer freely agrees.'),C('willing.s2','自愿的','The rescue was made possible by willing donors who contributed without pressure.','救援得以完成，靠的是自願捐款且未受施壓的捐助者。','a willing participant / donation','Adjective: done by someone who has freely agreed, without reluctance.','The donors choose freely to contribute.')],[M('The willing volunteer was forced to stay late and strongly refused to help.','The reluctant volunteer was forced to stay late and refused to help.','A willing person is ready and agrees freely, not forced and resisting.')],[Q('willing.q1','willing.s1','meaning','Why did the volunteer stay late?','The volunteer freely agreed to help.','The volunteer refused and left early.','The volunteer was ordered to avoid the shelter.','Willing means ready to do something without force.'),Q('willing.q2','willing.s2','context','How did the donors contribute?','Freely and without pressure.','Only after threats.','Without knowing any money was given.','A willing contribution is freely chosen.'),Q('willing.q3','willing.s1','distinction','Which worker is willing?','One who agrees to take an extra shift.','One who is forced and protests.','One who cannot be contacted.','Agreement indicates readiness.'),Q('willing.q4','willing.s2','word-choice','Choose the voluntary-action use.','The willing participants signed up without pressure.','She was willing to stay and help.','The volunteer was willing to answer questions.','The first describes freely agreed participation.')]);
P('willingly','From willing + -ly; it means doing something happily or freely rather than under pressure.',[C('willingly.s1','欣然地；自愿地','The witness willingly shared the photographs with the family.','證人欣然把照片分享給家人。','agree / help / participate willingly','Adverb: in a way showing someone is happy to do something.','The witness chooses to share them.')],[M('The witness willingly shared the photos only after being threatened and forced to do so.','The witness unwillingly shared the photos after being threatened.','Willingly implies choice or eagerness, not coercion.')],[Q('willingly.q1','willingly.s1','meaning','How did the witness share the photos?','Freely and happily.','Only after being forced.','Without sharing them at all.','Willingly means gladly or freely.'),Q('willingly.q2','willingly.s1','context','Which person participates willingly?','Someone who volunteers without being pressured.','Someone compelled by threats.','Someone who refuses every request.','Voluntary participation is willing.'),Q('willingly.q3','willingly.s1','distinction','Which adverb contrasts with willingly?','Reluctantly','Gladly','Freely','Reluctantly indicates resistance rather than readiness.'),Q('willingly.q4','willingly.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct use.','He willingly returned the lost wallet to its owner.','He willingly returned it only because a threat forced him.','He willingly kept it and refused to give it back.','The first describes a freely chosen action.')]);
P('willingness','From willing + -ness; it names readiness to act when asked or when a need arises.',[C('willingness.s1','乐意','The manager praised the staff’s willingness to learn the new safety procedure.','經理稱讚員工樂於學習新的安全程序。','willingness to help / learn','Noun: readiness to do something if it is needed or asked.','The staff are ready to learn.')],[M('Her willingness to help was clear because she refused every request and offered no assistance.','Her unwillingness to help was clear because she refused every request.','Refusing all requests shows unwillingness, not readiness.')],[Q('willingness.q1','willingness.s1','meaning','What quality did the manager praise?','Readiness to learn the new procedure.','A refusal to learn anything.','A wide selection of procedures.','Willingness is readiness to do something.'),Q('willingness.q2','willingness.s1','context','Which action shows willingness to help?','Offering to carry boxes when asked.','Ignoring the request and walking away.','Agreeing only after threats.','The offer shows readiness to assist.'),Q('willingness.q3','willingness.s1','distinction','What does willingness measure?','Whether someone is ready to act.','How wide a doorway is.','How many windows a room has.','Willingness concerns readiness or consent.'),Q('willingness.q4','willingness.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','Her willingness to cooperate helped settle the dispute.','Her willingness refusing every proposal settled it.','Her width to cooperate helped settle it.','Willingness to cooperate means readiness to work together.')]);
P('willow','From Old English welig, the name of a tree with long hanging branches; willow wood is also used for objects.',[C('willow.s1','柳树','A willow leaned over the stream, its branches brushing the water.','一棵柳樹傾向溪流，枝條輕拂水面。','a weeping willow / willow tree','Noun: a tree with long, thin branches that hang down, often near water.','The tree’s branches droop toward the stream.'),C('willow.s2','柳木制品','The cricket bat was made from willow and polished before the match.','這支板球球棒由柳木製成，賽前已經打磨。','willow bat / basket','Noun: an object such as a bat or basket made from willow wood.' ,'The bat is made from the tree’s wood.'),C('willow.s3','柳木制的','A willow basket held apples from the orchard.','一個柳木編籃裝著果園裡的蘋果。','willow basket / furniture','Adjective: made from the wood of a willow tree.','The basket is made of willow material.')],[M('The willow beside the stream was a metal tool with no branches or leaves.','The metal tool was not a willow tree.','A willow is a tree, not a metal tool.')],[Q('willow.q1','willow.s1','meaning','What leaned over the stream?','A tree with long hanging branches.','A metal tool.','A wheat field.','Willow names a tree often growing near water.'),Q('willow.q2','willow.s2','context','What was the cricket bat made from?','Willow wood.','A willow tree’s leaves.','A metal window frame.','Willow can name the wood used to make a bat.'),Q('willow.q3','willow.s3','distinction','What does “willow basket” mean?','A basket made from willow material.','A basket containing a whole living tree.','A basket shaped like a window.','Here willow modifies basket and names its material.'),Q('willow.q4','willow.s1','word-choice','Choose the tree sense.','A willow shaded the stream with its drooping branches.','The bat was carved from willow.','The basket was made of willow.','The first is a living tree.')]);
P('willpower','From will + power; it is the ability to control impulses or keep doing something difficult.',[C('willpower.s1','意志力','She used willpower to finish the long rehabilitation exercises each morning.','她靠意志力每天早上完成漫長的復健訓練。','have / show / summon willpower','Noun: ability to make yourself do something difficult or resist a wish.','She persists despite effort and discomfort.')],[M('He showed willpower by giving in to every temptation and abandoning his goal immediately.','He lacked willpower because he gave in to every temptation and abandoned his goal.','Willpower means self-control and persistence, not yielding at once.')],[Q('willpower.q1','willpower.s1','meaning','What helped her finish the difficult exercises?','Self-control and determination.','A legal testament.','A wide doorway.','Willpower helps someone persist or resist impulses.'),Q('willpower.q2','willpower.s1','context','Which action shows willpower?','Turning down a tempting snack to keep a health goal.','Giving in to every temptation.','Stopping the goal at the first difficulty.','Resisting a wish demonstrates willpower.'),Q('willpower.q3','willpower.s1','distinction','What does willpower help a person do?','Continue a hard task despite discomfort.','Measure a material’s width.','Predict tomorrow’s weather.','It is mental strength to persist.'),Q('willpower.q4','willpower.s1','word-choice','Choose the natural phrase.','It took willpower to study instead of checking messages.','His willpower was the document leaving property to heirs.','The willpower measured the window.','The first describes self-control.')]);
P('wilt','From Old English wiltan, “become limp”; it describes a plant drooping or a person losing strength or confidence.',[C('wilt.s1','枯萎；变蔫','The lettuce began to wilt after two days without water.','萵苣兩天沒澆水後開始變蔫。','plants wilt; wilt in heat','Verb: of a plant, become limp from heat or lack of water; of a person, lose strength or confidence.','The leaves droop as they lose water.')],[M('The lettuce wilted in the heat by becoming crisp, firm, and more hydrated.','The lettuce stayed fresh after it was watered and kept cool.','Wilt means become limp or droop, not grow crisp and hydrated.')],[Q('wilt.q1','wilt.s1','meaning','What happened to the lettuce without water?','Its leaves became limp.','It became a willow tree.','It grew more hydrated and firm.','Plants wilt when they lose water and droop.'),Q('wilt.q2','wilt.s1','context','How did the speaker respond to harsh criticism?','The speaker’s confidence began to fade.','The speaker’s confidence grew stronger at once.','The speaker measured a window.','People can wilt figuratively by losing confidence.'),Q('wilt.q3','wilt.s1','distinction','Which plant is wilting?','A drooping plant in hot dry soil.','A firm plant just watered.','A branch woven into wicker.','Drooping indicates wilting.'),Q('wilt.q4','wilt.s1','word-choice','Choose the literal plant use.','The flowers wilted in the afternoon sun.','Her courage wilted after the defeat.','The lettuce wilted under criticism.','The first describes plants becoming limp.')]);
P('win','From Old English winnan, “strive or fight”; it means succeed in a contest, obtain something through effort, or a victory.',[C('win.s1','获胜；打败','The local team won the final match by two points.','當地球隊以兩分之差贏得決賽。','win a game / match / race','Verb: be first or best in a contest, or defeat an opponent.','The team defeats its opponent.'),C('win.s2','赢得；获得','Her careful research won the committee’s support for the restoration plan.','她仔細的研究為修復計畫贏得了委員會的支持。','win a prize / support / trust','Verb: get a prize, support, or result through effort or success.','The research persuades the committee.'),C('win.s3','胜利','The team celebrated its first win of the season.','球隊慶祝本季首場勝利。','a narrow / decisive win','Noun: a success in a game or contest.','The result is a victory.')],[M('The team won the final by losing by twenty points and finishing last.','The team lost the final by twenty points and finished last.','Winning means succeeding or defeating the opponent, not finishing last.')],[Q('win.q1','win.s1','meaning','How did the local team win the final?','It scored two more points than its opponent.','It finished last.','It withdrew before the match.','Win means succeed in or defeat an opponent in a contest.'),Q('win.q2','win.s2','context','What did the research obtain for the restoration plan?','The committee’s support.','A loss in the final.','A wider river.','Win can mean gain support through effort.'),Q('win.q3','win.s3','distinction','What did the team celebrate?','A victory in a contest.','A research method.','A tree’s branches.','Win as a noun means success in a contest.'),Q('win.q4','win.s1','word-choice','Choose the competition verb use.','She won the chess match after a long game.','Her evidence won public support.','The club recorded a win.','The first directly describes succeeding in a match.')]);
P('win over','From win + over; it means persuade someone who disagrees to support or agree with you.',[C('win over.s1','争取支持','The candidate won over skeptical residents by answering questions about the budget.','候選人回答了居民對預算的疑問，爭取到原本持懷疑態度的居民支持。','win someone over','Phrasal verb: persuade someone who disagreed to support or agree with you.','The residents change their position after hearing answers.')],[M('The candidate won over the skeptical residents by making them more opposed and less willing to support the plan.','The candidate failed to win over the skeptical residents because they became more opposed.','To win someone over is to persuade them toward support, not increase opposition.')],[Q('win over.q1','win over.s1','meaning','How did the candidate gain residents’ support?','By answering their budget questions.','By refusing to speak with them.','By widening the road.','Win over means persuade someone to support you.'),Q('win over.q2','win over.s1','context','What happened to the skeptical committee?','It was persuaded to agree with the proposal.','It became more opposed.','It won a sports match.','The members change from disagreement toward agreement.'),Q('win over.q3','win over.s1','distinction','Which action can win a customer over?','Addressing their concerns until they choose the product.','Ignoring their concerns and ending the conversation.','Announcing that they must buy it.','Persuasion changes someone’s view voluntarily.'),Q('win over.q4','win over.s1','grammar','Where does the object go in “win over the voters”?','Between win and over, or after win over.','Only before win.','Only after the sentence ends.','The separable phrasal verb allows “win the voters over.”')]);
P('wind','From Old English wind, “moving air”; the homograph verb comes from Old English windan, “twist or turn,” and also describes a road’s bends.',[C('wind.s1','风','A cold wind pushed fallen leaves across the empty field.','一陣冷風吹著落葉掠過空曠田野。','a strong / cold wind','Noun: air moving across land or sea.','Moving air carries the leaves.'),C('wind.s2','气息；腹气','After the steep climb, he was out of wind; the medicine also reduced stomach wind.','爬完陡坡後，他喘不過氣；藥物也減少了腹部脹氣。','be out of wind; stomach wind','Noun: breath needed for physical effort, or gas in the stomach.','The first phrase concerns breath after exertion.'),C('wind.s3','缠绕；上弦','Wind the loose cable around the reel before storing it.','收納前，把鬆散的電纜繞在捲軸上。','wind a cable / clock','Verb: wrap or turn something around and around.','The cable coils around the reel.'),C('wind.s4','蜿蜒','The path winds through the forest and follows the river bends.','小徑蜿蜒穿過森林，沿著河道轉彎。','a road / river winds through','Verb: of a road or river, bend many times.','The route curves repeatedly.')],[M('The road winds through the valley by running in one perfectly straight line without any bends.','The road runs straight through the valley without winding.','A road that winds bends repeatedly; a straight road does not.')],[Q('wind.q1','wind.s1','meaning','What pushed leaves across the field?','Moving air.','A cable around a reel.','A curving path.','Wind as a noun is moving air.'),Q('wind.q2','wind.s2','context','Why was the climber out of wind?','The steep climb left him short of breath.','The road curved through the forest.','A cable was wrapped around a reel.','Out of wind means lacking breath after effort.'),Q('wind.q3','wind.s3','distinction','What should happen to the loose cable?','It should be wrapped around the reel.','It should be left in a straight line.','It should be carried by a cold breeze.','Wind as a verb can mean coil around something.'),Q('wind.q4','wind.s4','word-choice','Choose the winding-road use.','The lane winds through the hills in several curves.','A cold wind crossed the hill.','He wound the cable onto a spool.','The first describes a road that bends repeatedly.')]);
P('windblown','From wind + blown; it describes something moved, shaped, or disheveled by the wind.',[C('windblown.s1','被风吹乱的','Her windblown hair fell across her face after the walk along the cliffs.','沿著懸崖散步後，她被風吹亂的頭髮垂到臉上。','windblown hair / sand / coast','Adjective: moved, shaped, or disheveled by wind.','The wind has moved her hair.')],[M('Her windblown hair stayed perfectly arranged because no air had touched it.','Her neatly arranged hair remained untouched by the wind.','Windblown describes something affected or displaced by wind.')],[Q('windblown.q1','windblown.s1','meaning','Why did her hair fall across her face?','Wind had blown it out of place.','She had just woven it into wicker.','It was frozen in a window.','Windblown means moved or disheveled by wind.'),Q('windblown.q2','windblown.s1','context','Which landscape is windblown?','A bare coastal ridge constantly exposed to strong winds.','A sheltered room with still air.','A paved road indoors.','The ridge is shaped or exposed by wind.'),Q('windblown.q3','windblown.s1','distinction','Which sand is windblown?','Sand swept into dunes by gusts.','Sand sealed in a glass jar.','Sand held underwater.','The wind has moved the sand.'),Q('windblown.q4','windblown.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate description.','The windblown grass leaned toward the east.','The windblown grass had never felt moving air.','The grass wound itself around a cable.','The first shows wind moving the grass.')]);
P('windmill','From wind + mill; it means a traditional building using wind to grind or pump, and informally a modern wind-powered turbine.',[C('windmill.s1','传统风车磨坊','The restored windmill ground grain using sails turned by the coastal breeze.','修復後的風車磨坊利用海風轉動風翼來磨穀物。','a historic / grain windmill','Noun: a building with sails that uses wind to grind grain or pump water.','The rotating sails power a mill.'),C('windmill.s2','风力发电机','A modern windmill on the ridge sends electricity to nearby homes.','山脊上的現代風力發電機把電力輸送給附近住家。','a windmill for generating electricity','Noun: a tower with blades that uses wind to produce electricity.','The blades drive an electric generator.')],[M('The historic windmill ground grain with no sails or moving parts and used only a diesel engine.','The historic windmill used wind-driven sails to grind grain.','A traditional windmill is powered by wind turning its sails.')],[Q('windmill.q1','windmill.s1','meaning','What powered the restored mill’s grain grinding?','Wind turning its sails.','A mobile phone.','A river’s width.','A traditional windmill uses wind-driven sails.'),Q('windmill.q2','windmill.s2','context','What does the modern windmill send to nearby homes?','Electricity generated by its blades.','Ground grain.','A warning sign.','Modern windmills can generate electricity.'),Q('windmill.q3','windmill.s1','distinction','Which windmill is a historic mill?','A building with sails that grind grain.','A tower whose blades send electricity to homes.','A handheld fan with no mill.','The first is the traditional grain mill.'),Q('windmill.q4','windmill.s2','word-choice','Choose the modern energy use.','The ridge turbine fed power from its windmill into the grid.','The old windmill ground wheat for villagers.','The windmill pumped water into a millpond.','The first refers to a modern electricity generator.')]);
P('window','From Old Norse vindauga, literally “wind eye”; it names a glass opening, a brief opportunity, or a framed computer area.',[C('window.s1','窗户','She opened the kitchen window to let the smoke out.','她打開廚房窗戶讓煙散出去。','open / close / look through a window','Noun: an opening in a wall or vehicle, usually fitted with glass.','The opening allows air and light through.'),C('window.s2','机会窗口','The crew had a narrow weather window to repair the antenna before the storm.','風暴來臨前，維修團隊只有短暫的好天氣窗口可以修理天線。','a window of opportunity / time','Noun: a short period when an action is possible.','The weather creates a brief chance.'),C('window.s3','电脑窗口','She dragged the spreadsheet window beside the map on her screen.','她把試算表視窗拖到螢幕地圖旁邊。','open / close / resize a window','Noun: a framed area on a computer screen for one program.','The window displays a program.')],[M('The crew had a weather window of six months to repair the antenna before the storm arrived tomorrow.','The crew had a narrow weather window before the storm arrived tomorrow.','A window of opportunity is a short period, not six months in this context.')],[Q('window.q1','window.s1','meaning','Why did she open the kitchen window?','To let smoke out.','To resize a computer program.','To widen the river.','A physical window is an opening in a wall or vehicle.'),Q('window.q2','window.s2','context','How long could the crew repair the antenna?','During a brief period of suitable weather.','At any time over the next six months.','Only in a computer program.','A weather window is a short opportunity.'),Q('window.q3','window.s3','distinction','What did she drag beside the map?','A spreadsheet area on the computer screen.','A glass pane in the kitchen.','A weather forecast outside.','A computer window frames a program.'),Q('window.q4','window.s2','word-choice','Choose the opportunity-period use.','We have a short window to submit the application.','The cat sat on the window ledge.','She closed the window on her screen.','The first means a brief time in which action is possible.')]);
P('windscreen','From wind + screen; chiefly British English for the large glass panel across the front of a car or other vehicle.',[C('windscreen.s1','挡风玻璃','A stone cracked the windscreen while the car traveled along the gravel road.','汽車沿碎石路行駛時，一顆石子打裂了擋風玻璃。','a cracked / heated windscreen','Noun: the large front window of a car or other vehicle.','The glass protects the driver and passengers from wind.')],[M('The driver looked through the windscreen, which was the car’s rear tire rather than its front glass.','The driver looked through the windscreen, the large glass panel at the front of the car.','A windscreen is the front glass, not a tire.')],[Q('windscreen.q1','windscreen.s1','meaning','What did the stone crack?','The large glass panel at the front of the car.','The rear tire.','The side mirror only.','Windscreen is the front vehicle window.'),Q('windscreen.q2','windscreen.s1','context','Where does a driver look through a windscreen?','Through the glass at the front of the vehicle.','Through a phone app.','Through the rear wheel.','The windscreen protects and provides forward visibility.'),Q('windscreen.q3','windscreen.s1','distinction','Which term is commonly used for this part in British English?','Windscreen','Wicker','Wilderness','Windscreen is the British term for the vehicle’s front window.'),Q('windscreen.q4','windscreen.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate repair use.','The mechanic replaced the cracked windscreen.','The mechanic replaced the cracked willow.','The mechanic widened the car’s width.','A cracked vehicle front glass can be replaced.')]);P('windswept','From wind + swept; it describes a place exposed to wind or hair and clothes blown out of place.',[C('windswept.s1','当风的；被风吹乱的','The windswept headland had few trees, and her hair blew across her eyes.','迎風的海岬幾乎沒有樹木，她的頭髮也被吹到眼前。','a windswept coast / hill / look','Adjective: open to wind, or visibly blown about by it.','Both the headland and her hair are affected by wind.')],[M('The windswept beach was sheltered from every breeze, and all the grass stood perfectly still.','The exposed beach was windswept, with grass bent by the gusts.','Windswept describes exposure to wind, not complete shelter from it.')],[Q('windswept.q1','windswept.s1','meaning','Why were few trees growing on the headland?','It was exposed to strong winds.','It was sheltered from all air.','It was covered by a roof.','A windswept place is open to wind.'),Q('windswept.q2','windswept.s1','context','What happened to her hair?','The wind blew it across her eyes.','It was woven into a basket.','It became a glass panel.','Hair can look windswept after being blown about.'),Q('windswept.q3','windswept.s1','distinction','Which scene is windswept?','Grass bends on an exposed ridge in a gale.','Leaves stay still in a sealed room.','A hill is sheltered behind a wall.','The ridge is plainly affected by wind.'),Q('windswept.q4','windswept.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate phrase.','a windswept cliff path','a windswept room with no moving air','a windscreen made of hair','The cliff path is open to wind.')]);
P('wine','From Old English wīn, from Latin vīnum; it names an alcoholic drink made by fermenting grapes or other fruit, or a kind or serving of it.',[C('wine.s1','葡萄酒；果酒','The winery fermented local grapes into a dry red wine.','酒莊把當地葡萄發酵成乾型紅酒。','red / white / sparkling wine','Noun: an alcoholic drink made by fermenting grapes or other fruit.','Fermentation turns the grapes into an alcoholic drink.'),C('wine.s2','一种酒；一杯酒','The menu offers a local wine by the glass with the cheese course.','菜單提供一款當地酒，可搭配起司套餐按杯點選。','a wine from a region; a glass of wine','Noun: a particular variety of wine or one serving of it.','The phrase refers to a variety and a serving.')],[M('The grape wine was made by boiling the fruit without fermentation and contained no alcohol.','The grape wine was made by fermenting the fruit into an alcoholic drink.','Wine in this sense is an alcoholic drink made by fermentation.')],[Q('wine.q1','wine.s1','meaning','How did the winery make the red wine?','By fermenting local grapes.','By weaving grapevines into wicker.','By freezing plain water.','Wine is produced from fermented fruit.'),Q('wine.q2','wine.s2','context','What can a customer order by the glass?','A serving of a local wine.','A whole vineyard.','A metal wire.','Wine can mean one serving.'),Q('wine.q3','wine.s1','distinction','Which drink is wine?','An alcoholic drink made by fermenting grapes.','Fresh grape juice that was never fermented.','A glass used to serve water.','Fermentation distinguishes wine from unfermented juice.'),Q('wine.q4','wine.s2','word-choice','Choose the variety sense.','The restaurant stocks a wine from the northern valley.','The grapes were fermented into wine.','The vintner harvested the grapes.','The first points to a particular kind of wine.')]);
P('wing','From Old English wenge, related to Old Norse vængir; it names a flying appendage, an aircraft surface, a side part or faction, and the phrasal use “wing it” means improvise.',[C('wing.s1','翅膀；翼','The injured gull held one wing close to its body.','受傷的海鷗把一側翅膀緊貼身體。','a bird / insect wing','Noun: an appendage used by a bird, bat, or insect to fly.' ,'The gull’s appendage is injured.'),C('wing.s2','机翼','The engineer inspected a crack beneath the left wing of the aircraft.','工程師檢查飛機左側機翼下方的裂縫。','an aircraft wing','Noun: a flat projecting part of an aircraft that helps it fly.','The part belongs to the plane.'),C('wing.s3','侧翼；侧厅','The museum added a new wing for its collection of modern art.','博物館增建了一座側翼，用來展示現代藝術收藏。','a hospital / museum wing; the left wing','Noun: a side section of a building or one side of a political group.' ,'The new galleries form a side section.'),C('wing.s4','即兴应付','I had no time to prepare, so I had to wing the short presentation.','我沒有時間準備，只好即興完成這場簡短簡報。','wing it','Verb phrase: perform or speak without preparation.' ,'The speaker improvises.')],[M('She had rehearsed the presentation for weeks, but said she would wing it because she had prepared every line.','She had not prepared and had to wing the presentation.','To wing it is to improvise without preparation, not recite a rehearsed script.')],[Q('wing.q1','wing.s1','meaning','What did the injured gull hold close to its body?','A flying appendage.','A museum gallery.','A presentation.','A bird’s wing is its flying appendage.'),Q('wing.q2','wing.s2','context','Where did the engineer find a crack?','Beneath the aircraft’s left flying surface.','In the museum’s new gallery.','In the speaker’s notes.','An aircraft wing helps it fly.'),Q('wing.q3','wing.s3','distinction','What did the museum add?','A side section for modern art.','A bird’s feather.','An unprepared speech.','A building wing is a side section.'),Q('wing.q4','wing.s4','word-choice','What does “wing the presentation” mean here?','Speak without preparing it in advance.','Inspect the airplane.','Build another museum section.','“Wing it” means improvise.')]);
P('wingless','From wing + -less, “without”; it describes a creature or device that has no wings.',[C('wingless.s1','没有翅膀的','The wingless worker ant traveled through the narrow tunnel beneath the nest.','沒有翅膀的工蟻穿過蟻巢下方狹窄的通道。','a wingless insect / bird','Adjective: having no wings.','The ant has no wings.')],[M('The wingless ant crossed the tunnel by beating its two broad wings to lift off.','The wingless ant crawled through the tunnel because it had no wings.','Wingless means lacking wings, so the ant cannot beat wings it does not have.')],[Q('wingless.q1','wingless.s1','meaning','How did the worker ant travel?','It crawled through the tunnel without wings.','It flew on broad wings.','It sailed on a boat.','Wingless means having no wings.'),Q('wingless.q2','wingless.s1','context','Which animal is wingless?','A worker ant with no wings.','A butterfly with two wings.','A bird gliding overhead.','The ant lacks wings.'),Q('wingless.q3','wingless.s1','distinction','What does the suffix in wingless indicate?','The absence of wings.','A very large wing.','A wing used for steering.','The suffix -less means without.'),Q('wingless.q4','wingless.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate description.','A wingless insect crawled under the stone.','A wingless insect flew on broad wings.','A wingless bird flapped its wings.','The first is consistent with having no wings.')]);
P('wingspan','From wing + span; it is the distance across a bird’s or aircraft’s wings when fully extended.',[C('wingspan.s1','翼展','The albatross has a wingspan of more than three metres when its wings are spread.','信天翁展開雙翼時，翼展超過三公尺。','a wingspan of + measurement','Noun: the distance from one wingtip to the other across fully spread wings.','The measurement runs across the spread wings.')],[M('The albatross’s wingspan measured from its beak to its tail, not from one wingtip to the other.','The albatross’s wingspan measured from one wingtip to the other.','Wingspan measures across the wings, not along the body.')],[Q('wingspan.q1','wingspan.s1','meaning','What did the three-metre figure measure?','The distance across the bird’s spread wings.','Its body length from beak to tail.','Its nest’s width.','Wingspan measures from wingtip to wingtip.'),Q('wingspan.q2','wingspan.s1','context','When is wingspan measured?','When the wings are fully extended.','When the bird is asleep with wings folded.','When the bird is swimming underwater.','The wings are spread for the measurement.'),Q('wingspan.q3','wingspan.s1','distinction','Which measurement is a wingspan?','The distance from one aircraft wingtip to the other.','The length of the runway.','The thickness of one feather.','The first measures across an aircraft’s wings.'),Q('wingspan.q4','wingspan.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct description.','The eagle’s wingspan reached two metres.','The eagle’s wingspan was its beak-to-tail length only.','The eagle’s wingspan measured its nest’s depth.','The first gives a cross-wing measurement.')]);
P('wink','From Old English wincian, “close one eye”; it is a quick one-eye signal, the act itself, or a very brief moment.',[C('wink.s1','眨眼；使眼色','She gave the goalkeeper a quick wink before taking the penalty kick.','罰點球前，她迅速對守門員眨了一下眼。','give / shoot someone a wink','Verb: close one eye briefly, often as a signal.' ,'She makes a brief one-eye signal.'),C('wink.s2','眼色；眨眼','His wink told the children that the surprise party was still secret.','他的眼色告訴孩子們，驚喜派對仍要保密。','a quick wink; with a wink','Noun: one quick closing of an eye, often as a signal.' ,'The gesture communicates silently.'),C('wink.s3','片刻；一點睡眠','The night-shift nurse did not get a wink of sleep during the busy ward round.','夜班護士在忙碌的病房巡視期間一點睡眠也沒有。','not get a wink of sleep','Noun: a very short period, especially a moment of sleep.' ,'The phrase means no sleep at all.')],[M('He did not get a wink of sleep, meaning he slept soundly for eight uninterrupted hours.','He did not get a wink of sleep, meaning he slept not at all.','“Not get a wink of sleep” is an emphatic negative idiom.')],[Q('wink.q1','wink.s1','meaning','What did she do before the penalty kick?','She briefly closed one eye as a signal.','She slept through the match.','She waved both arms.','To wink is to close one eye briefly.'),Q('wink.q2','wink.s2','context','How did the children know the party remained secret?','His brief eye signal told them.','He shouted the surprise aloud.','He closed the stadium.','A wink can communicate a message.'),Q('wink.q3','wink.s3','distinction','What does “not get a wink of sleep” mean?','Not sleep at all.','Sleep for one full week.','Close one eye as a signal.','The phrase uses wink for a tiny bit of sleep.'),Q('wink.q4','wink.s1','word-choice','Choose the verb use.','She winked at her teammate from across the room.','He did not get a wink of sleep.','The signal was a knowing wink.','The first describes the action of closing one eye.')]);
P('winner','From win + -er, “one who wins”; it means a person or thing that wins, or someone or something likely to succeed.',[C('winner.s1','获胜者；赢家','The winner of the final received a silver cup from the mayor.','決賽的獲勝者從市長手中接過銀盃。','the winner of a race / prize','Noun: a person, team, or thing that wins a competition or prize.' ,'The person won the final.'),C('winner.s2','成功者；成功之选','The simple repair proved a winner because it saved money and lasted for years.','這項簡單的修理很成功，既省錢又維持多年。','a real / likely winner','Noun: a person or thing that is successful or likely to succeed.' ,'The repair has proved successful.')],[M('The winner of the final was the team that lost every round and received no prize.','The winner of the final was the team that took the title.','A winner wins; a team that loses every round is not the winner.')],[Q('winner.q1','winner.s1','meaning','Who received the silver cup?','The person who won the final.','The team eliminated first.','The mayor’s assistant who lost.','A winner is the person or team that wins.'),Q('winner.q2','winner.s2','context','Why was the repair called a winner?','It saved money and lasted for years.','It failed immediately and cost more.','It won a foot race.','A thing can be a winner if it proves successful.'),Q('winner.q3','winner.s1','distinction','Which is a winner in a competition?','The entrant awarded first place.','An entrant who withdrew before starting.','A spectator who did not compete.','The first won the competition.'),Q('winner.q4','winner.s2','word-choice','Choose the “successful choice” sense.','The low-cost plan was a winner with customers.','The runner was the winner of the race.','The trophy was handed to the race winner.','The first describes a successful option.')]);
P('winter','From Old English winter, probably related to a root meaning “wet season”; it names the coldest season or the act of spending that season somewhere.',[C('winter.s1','冬天；冬季','The lake usually freezes during winter, between autumn and spring.','湖面通常在秋春之間的冬季結冰。','in / during winter; a cold winter','Noun: the coldest season of the year.' ,'The sentence names the season.'),C('winter.s2','过冬；在某处度过冬天','The migrating cranes winter in wetlands south of the mountain range.','候鳥在山脈以南的濕地度過冬季。','winter in / somewhere','Verb: spend the winter in a particular place.' ,'The cranes spend the season there.')],[M('The cranes winter in the southern wetlands, meaning they spend the cold season there only in summer.','The cranes winter in the southern wetlands, meaning they spend the cold season there.','To winter somewhere means to spend winter there, not summer.')],[Q('winter.q1','winter.s1','meaning','When does the lake usually freeze?','During the coldest season, between autumn and spring.','During midsummer.','Only during a single afternoon.','Winter is the coldest season.'),Q('winter.q2','winter.s2','context','Where do the cranes spend the cold season?','In wetlands south of the mountains.','On the lake only in summer.','In a wicker basket.','To winter in a place is to spend winter there.'),Q('winter.q3','winter.s1','distinction','Which phrase uses winter as a season noun?','The road closes during winter.','The cranes winter in the marsh.','The birds are wintering south.','The first names the season.'),Q('winter.q4','winter.s2','word-choice','Choose the verb sense.','Many geese winter along the warm coast.','Winter brings ice to the lake.','The coldest winter lasted three months.','The first means spend winter in a location.')]);
P('wintertime','From winter + time; it names the period of the year when winter occurs.',[C('wintertime.s1','冬季；冬天','At wintertime, the village lights lanterns along the snowy main street.','冬季時，村民會在積雪的主街掛起燈籠。','at / during wintertime','Noun: the period of the year when it is winter.' ,'The lantern event happens during the winter season.')],[M('The village held its wintertime lantern festival in midsummer, during the hottest week of the year.','The village held its wintertime lantern festival during the cold winter season.','Wintertime is the period when it is winter, not midsummer.')],[Q('wintertime.q1','wintertime.s1','meaning','When does the village light its lanterns?','During the winter season.','At midsummer.','During a spring harvest.','Wintertime is the period when it is winter.'),Q('wintertime.q2','wintertime.s1','context','What does “at wintertime” refer to?','The time of year when winter occurs.','The exact hour of sunrise.','A period of summer heat.','The word names a season’s period.'),Q('wintertime.q3','wintertime.s1','distinction','Which event happens at wintertime?','A festival held during the snowy cold season.','A festival held only in midsummer.','A harvest held in autumn.','The first event fits wintertime.'),Q('wintertime.q4','wintertime.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct use.','At wintertime, daylight is short in the north.','At wintertime, it is the height of midsummer.','Wintertime means one minute on a clock.','The first connects the period with winter conditions.')]);
P('wintry','From winter + -y; it describes winter-like cold weather or a cold, unfriendly manner or appearance.',[C('wintry.s1','寒冷如冬的','A wintry rain swept across the station platform, and every passenger tightened a coat.','寒冷如冬的雨掃過車站月台，每位乘客都把外套裹緊。','wintry weather / wind / sky','Adjective: cold or otherwise characteristic of winter.' ,'The cold rain resembles winter weather.'),C('wintry.s1','冷淡的；阴郁的','He offered a wintry smile that showed little warmth after the argument.','爭吵後，他露出冷淡的笑容，幾乎沒有親切感。','a wintry smile / manner','Adjective: figuratively cold or unfriendly.' ,'The smile is emotionally cold.')],[M('She gave him a wintry smile full of warmth and affection, welcoming him as a close friend.','She gave him a wintry smile that seemed cold and unfriendly.','The figurative sense of wintry suggests emotional coldness, not warmth.')],[Q('wintry.q1','wintry.s1','meaning','Why did passengers tighten their coats?','Cold rain made the weather feel like winter.','The platform was heated by summer sun.','They were about to swim.','Wintry can describe cold winter-like weather.'),Q('wintry.q2','wintry.s1','context','What did his smile suggest?','He was emotionally cold after the argument.','He felt warm affection.','He was laughing loudly.','A wintry smile can be unfriendly.'),Q('wintry.q3','wintry.s1','distinction','Which is wintry weather?','Cold rain under a grey winter sky.','A hot and humid tropical afternoon.','A warm indoor room.','The first has winter-like cold.'),Q('wintry.q4','wintry.s1','word-choice','Choose the figurative use.','She answered with a wintry look and no greeting.','A wintry wind froze the lake.','The wintertime festival opened.','The first describes an unfriendly manner.')]);
P('wipe','From Old English wīpian, “rub”; it means rub a surface clean or dry, remove something completely, or a single rub/cleaning cloth.',[C('wipe.s1','擦；拭；抹','Please wipe the wet table with a clean cloth before setting out the plates.','請先用乾淨抹布擦乾濕桌面，再擺放餐盤。','wipe a surface with a cloth','Verb: rub a surface to clean or dry it.' ,'The cloth removes water from the table.'),C('wipe.s2','彻底清除','The technician will wipe the old files from the encrypted drive.','技術人員會從加密硬碟中徹底清除舊檔案。','wipe data / files from a device','Verb: remove information or a group completely.' ,'The files will be deleted.'),C('wipe.s3','一擦；湿巾','She cleaned the small cut with one antiseptic wipe from the first-aid kit.','她用急救箱裡的一片消毒濕巾清理小傷口。','an antiseptic / wet wipe; give something a wipe','Noun: one act of rubbing, or a small cloth used for cleaning.' ,'The small cleaning cloth is a wipe.')],[M('The technician promised to wipe the files from the drive, but left every file untouched and fully recoverable.','The technician wiped the files from the drive so they could no longer be accessed.','To wipe files is to remove them, not leave them untouched.')],[Q('wipe.q1','wipe.s1','meaning','What should be done to the wet table?','Rub it dry with a clean cloth.','Delete its files.','Cover it with a roof.','Wipe a surface by rubbing it clean or dry.'),Q('wipe.q2','wipe.s2','context','What will the technician do to the old files?','Remove them completely from the drive.','Rub the screen with a wet cloth only.','Print another copy.','Wipe data means erase it.'),Q('wipe.q3','wipe.s3','distinction','What did she use on the cut?','A small antiseptic cleaning cloth.','A computer drive.','A glass window.','A wipe can be a small cleaning cloth.'),Q('wipe.q4','wipe.s1','word-choice','Choose the surface-cleaning verb.','He wiped mud from the boots with a rag.','She wiped the database from the server.','He bought a packet of wipes.','The first is rubbing a surface clean.')]);
P('wipe out','From wipe + out; it means destroy or remove completely, or defeat an opponent by a very large margin.',[C('wipe out.s1','彻底消灭；摧毁','The invasive beetle could wipe out the orchard if the trees were left untreated.','若不處理，這種入侵甲蟲可能會毀掉整座果園。','wipe out a species / disease / population','Phrasal verb: destroy or remove something completely.' ,'The beetle threatens the whole orchard.'),C('wipe out.s2','大败','The visiting team wiped out its rivals by scoring six goals to none.','客隊以六比零大勝對手。','wipe out an opponent in a match','Phrasal verb: defeat an opponent decisively.' ,'The score shows a very large victory.')],[M('The beetles wiped out the orchard, but every tree remained healthy and none was damaged.','The beetles wiped out the orchard, leaving every tree dead.','Wipe out means destroy completely, so healthy untouched trees contradict the claim.')],[Q('wipe out.q1','wipe out.s1','meaning','What could the invasive beetle do?','Destroy the orchard completely.','Polish one leaf.','Score a goal for the visitors.','Wipe out can mean destroy completely.'),Q('wipe out.q2','wipe out.s2','context','What was the score in the match?','The visiting team won six goals to none.','The rivals won six to none.','The match was canceled before play.','The phrase can describe a decisive defeat.'),Q('wipe out.q3','wipe out.s1','distinction','Which event wipes out a population?','A disease kills every member of the isolated colony.','One animal is briefly startled.','A team wins by one point.','The first removes the population completely.'),Q('wipe out.q4','wipe out.s2','word-choice','Choose the sports use.','The champions wiped out their rivals, 8–1.','The storm wiped out the coastal village.','The clerk wiped out an old file.','The first means defeat by a large margin.')]);
P('wire','From Old English wīr, “metal wire”; it names a thin metal strand, an electrical conductor, an old telegraph message, or the act of connecting with wire.',[C('wire.s1','金属丝；铁丝','The jeweler bent a thin wire into a small frame for the pendant.','珠寶匠把細金屬絲彎成吊墜的小框架。','a strand / coil of wire','Noun: a long, thin piece of bendable metal.' ,'The wire is shaped into a frame.'),C('wire.s2','电线；电缆','An electrician replaced the damaged wire behind the wall socket.','電工更換了插座後方受損的電線。','electrical / telephone wire','Noun: a metal conductor that carries electricity or signals.' ,'The conductor carries electricity.'),C('wire.s3','电报（旧）','The editor received a wire from the overseas correspondent with breaking news.','編輯收到海外記者發來的電報，內容是突發新聞。','send / receive a wire','Noun: a message sent by telegraph.' ,'The message arrived by telegraph.'),C('wire.s4','给……接线','The crew will wire the new laboratory before its instruments are installed.','儀器安裝前，工程團隊會為新實驗室接好電線。','wire a building / device','Verb: connect a building or machine with electrical wire.' ,'The room is being connected to electrical conductors.')],[M('The electrician repaired the live wire by replacing it with a length of dry paper string that could not conduct electricity.','The electrician replaced the damaged wire with insulated copper cable.','An electrical wire must conduct electricity; paper string cannot serve as the damaged conductor.')],[Q('wire.q1','wire.s1','meaning','What did the jeweler bend into a pendant frame?','A thin strand of metal.','A telegraph message.','A glass pane.','Wire can mean thin bendable metal.'),Q('wire.q2','wire.s2','context','What did the electrician replace?','A damaged electrical conductor behind the socket.','A newspaper article.','A bird’s wing.','Electrical wire carries current or signals.'),Q('wire.q3','wire.s3','distinction','How did the editor receive the breaking news?','As a telegraph message from a correspondent.','As a metal frame for jewelry.','As electricity through a wall socket.','An older use of wire is a telegram.'),Q('wire.q4','wire.s4','word-choice','Choose the verb meaning “install electrical conductors.”','The crew wired the laboratory before installing equipment.','The jeweler shaped a wire into a loop.','The editor received a wire from overseas.','The first uses wire as a verb.')]);
P('wireless','From wire + -less; it describes communication or a device using radio waves rather than physical wires.',[C('wireless.s1','无线的','The wireless headphones connect to the tablet through a short-range radio signal.','這副無線耳機透過短距離無線電訊號連接平板。','wireless headphones / network / signal','Adjective: using radio waves rather than wires to communicate.' ,'The headphones link by radio.')],[M('The wireless headphones connected to the tablet through a cable plugged into both devices.','The wireless headphones connected to the tablet by radio without a cable.','Wireless communication does not require a physical connecting wire.')],[Q('wireless.q1','wireless.s1','meaning','How do the headphones connect?','By a short-range radio signal.','Through a cable joining both devices.','By winding copper around a reel.','Wireless devices communicate without a wire.'),Q('wireless.q2','wireless.s1','context','Which item is wireless?','Headphones that receive audio by radio.','A speaker connected only by a long cable.','A wire used to carry current.','The first uses radio rather than a physical cable.'),Q('wireless.q3','wireless.s1','distinction','What does “wireless network” imply?','Devices exchange data without a physical network cable.','All devices are made from metal wire.','The network has no signal.','Wireless describes radio communication.'),Q('wireless.q4','wireless.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct adjective.','The wireless sensor sent readings by radio.','The wireless sensor was tethered by a copper lead.','The sensor wound wire around itself.','The first fits communication without a cable.')]);
P('wirephoto','From wire + photo, a shortening of “wire photograph”; it is a picture transmitted by a news agency over telegraph or wire-service channels.',[C('wirephoto.s1','传真照片；电传照片','The newspaper printed a wirephoto of the rescue ship sent from the coast that morning.','報紙刊登了當日上午從海岸傳來的救援船電傳照片。','a wirephoto from a correspondent','Noun: a news photograph transmitted electronically over a wire service.' ,'The picture is transmitted from a distant correspondent.')],[M('The wirephoto reached the newspaper as a fresh picture, but no image had been transmitted and the newsroom only received a blank page.','The wirephoto arrived as an image transmitted by the news service.','A wirephoto is a transmitted photograph, not a blank page.')],[Q('wirephoto.q1','wirephoto.s1','meaning','How did the newspaper receive the rescue-ship picture?','It was transmitted through a wire service.','A painter recreated it by hand.','The ship mailed a wicker basket.','A wirephoto is transmitted as a news image.'),Q('wirephoto.q2','wirephoto.s1','context','What did the correspondent send?','A photograph of the rescue ship.','A metal cable.','A printed weather forecast without an image.','The term names a transmitted photo.'),Q('wirephoto.q3','wirephoto.s1','distinction','What makes a picture a wirephoto?','It is sent to a news outlet electronically over a wire service.','It is painted on a metal wire.','It is a photograph of a window.','Transmission through the news service is the defining feature.'),Q('wirephoto.q4','wirephoto.s1','word-choice','Choose the correct newsroom use.','The editor received a wirephoto from the distant bureau.','The editor repaired a wirephoto with a soldering iron.','The editor called a wire a wirephoto.','The first is a transmitted news photograph.')]);
P('wisdom','From Old English wīsdōm, “wise judgment”; it means sound judgment from knowledge and experience or the accumulated teachings of a tradition.',[C('wisdom.s1','智慧；明智','Her wisdom helped the council choose a fair compromise after hours of debate.','經過數小時辯論，她的智慧幫助議會選出公平的折衷方案。','show / exercise wisdom','Noun: the ability to make good judgments based on knowledge and experience.' ,'She judges the dispute well.'),C('wisdom.s2','学问；至理名言','The book gathers the wisdom of generations of traditional healers.','這本書彙集了世代傳承的傳統療癒知識。','the wisdom of a tradition / ages','Noun: accumulated knowledge, teaching, or sayings.' ,'The book collects inherited teachings.')],[M('The council’s wisdom led it to reject all evidence and choose the most unfair compromise available.','The council used its wisdom to weigh the evidence and choose a fair compromise.','Wisdom involves sound judgment, not ignoring evidence and choosing unfairly.')],[Q('wisdom.q1','wisdom.s1','meaning','How did her wisdom help the council?','It helped members choose a fair compromise.','It made them reject all evidence.','It repaired a wire.','Wisdom is good judgment based on knowledge.'),Q('wisdom.q2','wisdom.s2','context','What did the book gather?','Teachings accumulated by generations of healers.','One person’s brief wink.','A set of electrical wires.','Wisdom can mean inherited knowledge and teachings.'),Q('wisdom.q3','wisdom.s1','distinction','Which shows practical wisdom?','A mediator weighs evidence before recommending a fair solution.','A judge ignores all facts and guesses.','A person repeats a rumor without checking.','The first makes a careful, informed judgment.'),Q('wisdom.q4','wisdom.s2','word-choice','Choose the accumulated-teaching sense.','The proverb preserves the wisdom of the elders.','Her wisdom settled the argument fairly.','He wisely checked the figures.','The first refers to knowledge passed down.')]);
P('wise','From Old English wīs, “having good judgment”; it describes sound judgment, a sensible choice, or becoming aware of something.',[C('wise.s1','明智的；有智慧的','The wise mediator listened to both families before proposing a settlement.','明智的調解人先聽取兩個家庭的說法，再提出和解方案。','a wise person / leader','Adjective: able to judge well through knowledge and experience.' ,'The mediator acts with good judgment.'),C('wise.s2','明智的；可取的','It would be wise to save a copy before updating the shared file.','更新共用檔案前先存一份副本會比較明智。','it is wise to do something','Adjective: sensible or advisable in a particular situation.' ,'Saving a copy is prudent.'),C('wise.s3','知道；明白过来','The inspector soon got wise to the seller’s false certificates.','檢查員很快識破賣方的假證書。','get wise to something','Verb phrase: become aware of a trick, fact, or situation.' ,'The inspector discovers the fraud.')],[M('It was wise to overwrite the only copy before checking the update, so the team had no way to recover its data.','It was unwise to overwrite the only copy before checking the update.','Wise describes a sensible action; destroying the only backup is imprudent.')],[Q('wise.q1','wise.s1','meaning','Why did the mediator seem wise?','The mediator heard both families before judging.','The mediator chose a side without listening.','The mediator forged a certificate.','A wise person exercises sound judgment.'),Q('wise.q2','wise.s2','context','What would be wise before updating the file?','Save a copy first.','Delete the only copy.','Ignore the update notes.','That is a sensible precaution.'),Q('wise.q3','wise.s3','distinction','What happened when the inspector got wise to the seller?','The inspector became aware of the false certificates.','The inspector forgot the inspection.','The inspector printed a photograph.','“Get wise to” means discover or understand a trick.'),Q('wise.q4','wise.s2','word-choice','Choose the sensible-advice use.','It is wise to check the figures before signing.','The wise elder settled the dispute.','She got wise to the forged label.','The first says the action is advisable.')]);
P('wisely','From wise + -ly; it is an adverb meaning in a way that shows good judgment or makes a sensible choice.',[C('wisely.s1','明智地；高明地','The hikers wisely turned back when dark clouds gathered over the exposed ridge.','裸露山脊上方聚起烏雲時，健行者明智地折返。','choose / spend / act wisely','Adverb: with good judgment or in a sensible way.' ,'Turning back reduces danger.')],[M('The hikers wisely continued onto the exposed ridge during a lightning storm, ignoring every safety warning.','The hikers wisely turned back when lightning approached.','Ignoring a lightning threat is not a sound or sensible decision.')],[Q('wisely.q1','wisely.s1','meaning','What did the hikers do?','They made a sensible choice to turn back.','They ignored a lightning storm.','They repaired the ridge.','Wisely means with good judgment.'),Q('wisely.q2','wisely.s1','context','Why was turning back wise?','Dark clouds gathered over an exposed ridge.','The path was perfectly safe and clear.','They had reached their warm shelter.','The choice reduced exposure to danger.'),Q('wisely.q3','wisely.s1','distinction','Which action is done wisely?','A traveler checks the weather before crossing a pass.','A driver speeds through a closed road.','A hiker ignores a lightning warning.','The first is careful and well judged.'),Q('wisely.q4','wisely.s1','grammar','Which sentence uses the adverb modifying a verb?','They wisely saved the last clean copy.','Their wise decision saved the copy.','Wisdom saved the copy.','Wisely modifies the action “saved.”')]);
P('wish','From Old English wyscan, “desire”; it means want an unreal or unlikely change, express a hope for someone, want to do something, or a desire itself.',[C('wish.s1','但愿；希望','I wish the rain would stop before the outdoor concert begins.','我但願戶外音樂會開始前雨就停下來。','wish + past form / would','Verb: want a situation to be different, often unreal or unlikely.' ,'The rain has not stopped, but the speaker wants it to.'),C('wish.s2','祝；祝愿','We wish the newlyweds a joyful life together.','我們祝新婚夫婦白頭偕老。','wish someone luck / happiness','Verb: express hope that someone will have something good.' ,'The speaker offers a good hope.'),C('wish.s3','希望；想要','I wish to speak with the director before the meeting ends.','我希望在會議結束前與主任談談。','wish to do something','Verb: want or intend to do something, often formally.' ,'The speaker wants to speak.'),C('wish.s4','愿望；心愿','Her wish to see the northern lights finally came true.','她想看北極光的願望終於實現了。','a wish for / to do something','Noun: a desire or hope, or the thing desired.' ,'Seeing the lights was the desire.')],[M('I wish the storm would stop because it has already stopped and the sky is perfectly clear.','I wish the storm would stop because it is still raining.','This wish form expresses a desired change to a situation that is not yet true.')],[Q('wish.q1','wish.s1','meaning','What does the speaker want before the concert?','For the rain to stop.','For the rain to continue forever.','To cancel the sky.','Wish can express desire for a different situation.'),Q('wish.q2','wish.s2','context','What did the couple receive?','A hope for a joyful life.','A complaint about their wedding.','An instruction to leave.','To wish someone something is to express a hope for them.'),Q('wish.q3','wish.s3','distinction','What does the speaker want to do?','Speak with the director.','See the northern lights as a noun desire.','Stop someone else speaking.','“Wish to speak” means want to speak.'),Q('wish.q4','wish.s4','word-choice','Which sentence uses wish as a noun?','Her wish to travel was finally fulfilled.','I wish the train were on time.','We wish you success.','The first names a desire.')]);
P('wishes','From wish + -es; it is the third-person singular verb form and the plural noun for hopes or expressions of goodwill.',[C('wishes.s1','祝愿；祝福','The card wishes the retiring teacher health and happiness in her next chapter.','卡片祝願退休教師在新階段健康快樂。','someone wishes someone something','Verb: expresses a hope that somebody will have something good.' ,'The card expresses goodwill.'),C('wishes.s2','愿望；心愿','The grant will fund the students’ wishes to build a community garden.','這筆補助將資助學生們建立社區花園的願望。','one’s wishes; wishes to do something','Noun plural: things somebody hopes or wants to happen.' ,'The students share a desire to build the garden.')],[M('The card wishes the teacher misfortune and failure, expressing a hope that everything goes badly.','The card wishes the teacher health and happiness.','To wish someone something in this context is to express a positive hope, not ill will.')],[Q('wishes.q1','wishes.s1','meaning','What does the card express?','A hope for the teacher’s health and happiness.','A prediction that she will fail.','A demand that she return to work.','The verb wishes conveys a hope for someone.'),Q('wishes.q2','wishes.s2','context','What will the grant support?','The students’ desire to build a community garden.','A teacher’s retirement card.','A wireless headset.','Wishes can be the things people hope to do.'),Q('wishes.q3','wishes.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses wishes as a verb?','The note wishes the couple good fortune.','Her wishes include a long trip.','Their wishes were written on the board.','The first has a subject expressing goodwill.'),Q('wishes.q4','wishes.s2','word-choice','Choose the plural-noun sense.','The applicants listed their wishes for the project.','The card wishes them success.','She wishes to apply.','The first means the things they hope for.')]);
P('wispy','From wisp + -y; it describes something thin, delicate, or insubstantial, often in strands.',[C('wispy.s1','细丝般的','Wispy clouds drifted above the ridge in pale, almost transparent strands.','山脊上方飄著絲縷般淡薄、幾乎透明的雲。','wispy hair / clouds / smoke','Adjective: delicate and insubstantial, often appearing in thin strands.','The clouds are slight and threadlike.')],[M('The wispy smoke formed a dense, heavy wall that completely blocked the view.','The wispy smoke rose in a faint, thin strand.','Wispy describes something delicate and insubstantial, not dense and heavy.')],[Q('wispy.q1','wispy.s1','meaning','How did the clouds look above the ridge?','Thin, pale, and almost transparent.','Dense and solid like a wall.','Dark and made of stone.','Wispy describes delicate, insubstantial strands.'),Q('wispy.q2','wispy.s1','context','Which smoke is wispy?','A faint curl that quickly disappears.','A thick cloud that blocks all light.','A puddle of water.','The faint curl is thin and insubstantial.'),Q('wispy.q3','wispy.s1','distinction','What kind of hair is wispy?','Fine strands that look delicate and sparse.','A thick, dense mass of hair.','Hair made of metal wire.','Wispy hair appears in slight strands.'),Q('wispy.q4','wispy.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate description.','Wispy mist hung in thin veils over the field.','Wispy fog formed an opaque solid wall.','The mist was a metal windscreen.','The first fits a thin, insubstantial mist.')]);
P('wistful','From wist + -ful, “full of longing”; it describes gentle sadness or longing for something past or unattainable.',[C('wistful.s1','渴望而惆怅的；依依不舍的','He gave a wistful smile while looking at the photograph of his childhood home.','他望著童年故居的照片，露出惆悵而懷念的微笑。','a wistful look / smile / longing','Adjective: feeling gentle sadness while longing for something absent, past, or unattainable.','He misses a home from the past.')],[M('She looked wistful about the lost childhood home, laughing without a trace of longing or sadness.','She looked wistful as she remembered the childhood home she could no longer visit.','Wistful combines longing with gentle sadness, which the corrected context shows.')],[Q('wistful.q1','wistful.s1','meaning','Why did he smile wistfully at the photograph?','He longed for a home from his past.','He was angry at a new house.','He had never seen the photograph.','Wistful suggests gentle sadness and longing.'),Q('wistful.q2','wistful.s1','context','What feeling does her expression show?','A quiet longing for something she cannot regain.','A loud celebration of a present victory.','Indifference to every memory.','Wistful often concerns a past or unattainable thing.'),Q('wistful.q3','wistful.s1','distinction','Which response is wistful?','A soft sigh while recalling a friend who moved away.','A furious shout at a broken machine.','A cheerful greeting to a visitor.','The first blends longing with sadness.'),Q('wistful.q4','wistful.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate use.','He cast a wistful glance toward the closed school.','She felt wistful because she had no longing or sadness.','The wistful hammer drove a nail.','The first describes longing for something past.')]);
P('wit','From Old English wit(t), “understanding, mind”; it means clever humor, quick intelligence, or a person known for humorous remarks.',[C('wit.s1','风趣；妙语','Her dry wit made the long committee meeting unexpectedly entertaining.','她冷面而機智的妙語讓冗長的委員會會議意外地有趣。','dry / sharp / quick wit','Noun: the ability to make clever and funny remarks.','Her comments are humorous and clever.'),C('wit.s2','才智；机智','The climber kept his wits and found a safe route through the sudden fog.','登山者保持冷靜機智，在突如其來的濃霧中找到安全路線。','keep / use one’s wits','Noun: quick intelligence used to judge or cope with a situation.','Quick thinking helps in danger.'),C('wit.s3','才子；风趣的人','The salon invited a celebrated wit to entertain the guests after dinner.','沙龍邀請一位著名的風趣人物在晚餐後娛樂賓客。','a famous / celebrated wit','Noun: a person known for clever, funny remarks.','The person is known for humor.')],[M('The climber lost his wits in the fog by calmly studying the map and choosing the safest route.','The climber kept his wits by studying the map and choosing a safe route.','Keeping one’s wits means staying mentally alert; calm problem-solving is not losing them.')],[Q('wit.q1','wit.s1','meaning','Why did the meeting become entertaining?','Her clever humorous remarks enlivened it.','She repaired a window.','She stayed silent throughout.','Wit can mean the ability to make clever jokes.'),Q('wit.q2','wit.s2','context','What helped the climber in the fog?','Quick intelligence and calm judgment.','A funny remark only.','A person invited to a salon.','Keeping one’s wits means thinking clearly.'),Q('wit.q3','wit.s3','distinction','Who is “a celebrated wit”?','A person famous for clever humorous remarks.','A metal conductor.','A person who never speaks.','The noun can refer to a witty person.'),Q('wit.q4','wit.s1','word-choice','Choose the humor sense.','The playwright’s wit delighted the audience.','The hiker used his wits to find shelter.','The salon hired a wit for the evening.','The first refers to clever humor itself.')]);
P('witch','From Old English wicce, “female magician”; it means a woman believed in stories or older beliefs to use magic, or a person identifying with a modern nature religion.',[C('witch.s1','女巫；巫婆（故事或信仰中）','In the folktale, a witch turned the prince into a raven with a spell.','民間故事中，一名女巫施咒把王子變成了烏鴉。','a witch in a story / legend','Noun: a woman believed, especially in stories or old belief, to use magic.','The character practices magic in a tale.'),C('witch.s2','女巫（现代信仰身份）','The museum interviewed a witch who explained how her modern nature religion marks the seasons.','博物館訪問一位女巫，她介紹自己的現代自然信仰如何標記季節。','a practising witch; identify as a witch','Noun: a person, often a woman, who practises a modern nature religion called witchcraft.','The person describes a living religious identity.')],[M('The folktale’s witch was an ordinary accountant who never used magic or appeared in the story.','The folktale’s witch cast a spell that changed the prince into a raven.','In this story sense, the witch is the character who uses magic.')],[Q('witch.q1','witch.s1','meaning','What did the folktale witch do?','She cast a spell on the prince.','She repaired a radio.','She interviewed the museum.','The story sense is a woman believed to use magic.'),Q('witch.q2','witch.s2','context','What did the interviewed witch explain?','How her modern nature religion marks the seasons.','How she turned a prince into a raven.','How to install an electrical wire.','This sense can name a present-day religious identity.'),Q('witch.q3','witch.s1','distinction','Which use belongs to a fairy tale?','A witch places a spell on a sleeping castle.','A practitioner describes a seasonal ritual.','A person wins a sports final.','The first is a magical story character.'),Q('witch.q4','witch.s2','word-choice','Choose the modern identity use.','She identifies as a witch and follows a nature-based faith.','The witch in the legend turned the prince into a bird.','A wicked spell frightened the villagers.','The first identifies a person’s present religious practice.')]);
P('witchcraft','From witch + craft, “the practice of a witch”; it names the use or practice of magic, especially magic associated with witches.',[C('witchcraft.s1','巫术；魔法','The historical trial accused the healer of witchcraft, though the records show no evidence of harm.','歷史審判指控那位療癒師施行巫術，然而紀錄並未顯示傷害證據。','accuse someone of witchcraft; practise witchcraft','Noun: the practice of using magic powers, especially by a witch, often to do harm.','The trial concerns alleged magical practice.')],[M('The villagers called the healer’s work witchcraft, although it consisted only of ordinary gardening and contained no magic.','The villagers accused the healer of witchcraft, claiming she used magic to harm them.','Witchcraft refers to an alleged practice of magic, not ordinary gardening by itself.')],[Q('witchcraft.q1','witchcraft.s1','meaning','What did the historical trial accuse the healer of?','Using magic associated with a witch.','Growing ordinary vegetables only.','Repairing an aircraft wing.','Witchcraft names the practice of magic.'),Q('witchcraft.q2','witchcraft.s1','context','What was alleged in the records?','The healer used magic, supposedly to cause harm.','The healer transmitted a photograph.','The healer won a contest.','The definition concerns magical practice.'),Q('witchcraft.q3','witchcraft.s1','distinction','Which action would be called witchcraft in a legend?','Casting a spell to make a harvest fail.','Planting beans by ordinary methods.','Giving a neighbor a kind wish.','The first involves magic.'),Q('witchcraft.q4','witchcraft.s1','word-choice','Choose the appropriate use.','The novel describes witchcraft as a feared magical practice.','The novel called routine watering witchcraft despite no magic being involved.','The witchcraft was a wireless headset.','The first matches the established meaning.')]);
P('with','From Old English with, originally “against” and later “in company with”; it can express accompaniment, possession, instrument, cause, or opposition.',[C('with.s1','和……在一起；同……','Mina arrived with her brother and waited beside the entrance.','米娜和哥哥一同抵達，在入口旁等候。','with a person / group','Preposition: in the company of someone or something.','Her brother accompanies her.'),C('with.s2','带有；具有','The jacket with the silver buttons belongs to the costume department.','帶有銀色鈕扣的外套屬於服裝部。','a person / thing with a feature','Preposition: having or carrying a feature or object.','The jacket possesses the buttons.'),C('with.s3','用；以（工具或材料）','The carpenter tightened the screw with a small brass screwdriver.','木匠用一把小型黃銅螺絲起子鎖緊螺絲。','do something with a tool / material','Preposition: using a tool, means, or material.','The screwdriver is the instrument.'),C('with.s4','因；由于（某种情绪）','With relief, the doctor told the family that the operation had succeeded.','醫生如釋重負地告訴家屬，手術成功了。','with joy / anger / relief','Preposition: because of a feeling or condition.','Relief explains the doctor’s manner.'),C('with.s5','对；与……对抗','The small boat struggled with the current as it crossed the channel.','小船橫越水道時，奮力抵抗水流。','struggle / argue / compete with','Preposition: in relation to or in opposition to someone or something.','The current resists the boat.')],[M('The carpenter tightened the screw with a screwdriver, meaning he used the tool by ignoring it and working only with his bare feet.','The carpenter tightened the screw with a screwdriver, using it as the tool.','With in the tool sense identifies what is used to perform an action.')],[Q('with.q1','with.s1','meaning','Who accompanied Mina?','Her brother.','A silver button.','The current.','With can mean in someone’s company.'),Q('with.q2','with.s2','context','Which jacket belongs to the costume department?','The one that has silver buttons.','The one used to turn a screw.','The one fighting a current.','With can identify a possession or feature.'),Q('with.q3','with.s3','distinction','How did the carpenter tighten the screw?','By using a brass screwdriver.','Because of relief.','Against the current.','With names the instrument used.'),Q('with.q4','with.s5','word-choice','Which sentence uses with to show opposition?','The swimmer fought with the current.','Mina arrived with her brother.','The jacket came with silver buttons.','The first has with meaning in opposition to.')]);
P('withdraw','From with- + draw, “draw back”; it means retreat or leave, take money out of an account, or retract a statement or offer.',[C('withdraw.s1','撤退；退出；离开','The hikers withdrew from the exposed ridge when lightning appeared.','閃電出現時，健行者從裸露的山脊撤離。','withdraw from a place / contest','Verb: move back from a place or leave an activity.' ,'They leave the dangerous ridge.'),C('withdraw.s2','提取（存款）','She withdrew two hundred dollars from the ATM before the trip.','她出發前從提款機提領兩百元。','withdraw money from an account','Verb: take money out of a bank account.' ,'The money is taken from her account.'),C('withdraw.s3','撤回（言论、申请）','The newspaper withdrew its claim after finding that the photograph was misidentified.','發現照片辨識錯誤後，報社撤回了該項說法。','withdraw a claim / offer / application','Verb: state that a statement or offer is no longer valid.' ,'The paper retracts its claim.')],[M('She withdrew two hundred dollars from the ATM, leaving the money untouched in her bank account.','She withdrew two hundred dollars from the ATM, reducing the balance in her account.','To withdraw money is to take it out, not leave it untouched in the account.')],[Q('withdraw.q1','withdraw.s1','meaning','Why did the hikers leave the ridge?','Lightning made them retreat from danger.','They were depositing cash.','They were correcting a newspaper claim.','Withdraw can mean move back or leave.'),Q('withdraw.q2','withdraw.s2','context','What did she do at the ATM?','She took money out of her account.','She filed a legal claim.','She left a hiking contest.','Withdraw money means take it from a bank account.'),Q('withdraw.q3','withdraw.s3','distinction','What did the newspaper do after finding the error?','It retracted its claim.','It deposited cash.','It walked off a mountain.','Withdraw can mean retract a statement.'),Q('withdraw.q4','withdraw.s2','word-choice','Choose the bank sense.','He withdrew cash before the station closed.','The candidate withdrew from the race.','The company withdrew its offer.','The first concerns money leaving an account.')]);
P('withdrawal','From withdraw + -al; it can mean retracting something, taking money from a bank, retreating, leaving an activity, or removing funds or support.',[C('withdrawal.s1','撤回；收回','The newspaper issued a withdrawal of its inaccurate claim and printed a correction.','報社撤回了不實說法，並刊登更正。','a withdrawal of a claim / offer','Noun: the act of taking back something said, offered, or given.','The claim is taken back.'),C('withdrawal.s2','取款','A cash withdrawal appeared on her bank statement after the ATM visit.','她到提款機後，銀行對帳單上出現一筆現金提款。','make / request a withdrawal','Noun: the act of taking money from a bank account.','Money leaves the account.'),C('withdrawal.s3','撤退；撤出','The army began its withdrawal from the valley before the ceasefire expired.','停火協議到期前，軍隊開始撤出山谷。','a troop / military withdrawal','Noun: the act of moving an army or group away from a place.','The forces move away.'),C('withdrawal.s4','退出；退赛；退学','Her withdrawal from the tournament allowed the reserve player to take her place.','她退出錦標賽後，替補選手得以代替她參賽。','withdrawal from a contest / course','Noun: the act of leaving an activity, competition, or institution.','She leaves the competition.'),C('withdrawal.s5','资金或支持撤出','The withdrawal of grant funding forced the clinic to shorten its opening hours.','補助資金撤出後，診所被迫縮短營業時間。','withdrawal of funds / support','Noun: the act of taking money, support, or investment away from a project.','The project loses financial support.')],[M('The withdrawal of grant funding gave the clinic more money and support than before, so its budget increased.','The withdrawal of grant funding took financial support away and reduced the clinic’s budget.','A withdrawal removes money or support; it does not add to it.')],[Q('withdrawal.q1','withdrawal.s1','meaning','What did the newspaper retract?','Its inaccurate claim.','A cash machine.','The army’s route.','A withdrawal can be the act of taking back a statement.'),Q('withdrawal.q2','withdrawal.s2','context','What appeared on the bank statement?','A transaction taking cash out of the account.','A correction to a newspaper.','A military retreat.','A cash withdrawal takes money from a bank.'),Q('withdrawal.q3','withdrawal.s4','distinction','Why could the reserve player enter the tournament?','The first player left the competition.','The army left the valley.','The clinic lost a grant.','Withdrawal can mean leaving an event.'),Q('withdrawal.q4','withdrawal.s5','word-choice','Choose the funding sense.','The withdrawal of investment delayed the clinic expansion.','The withdrawal from the race was announced.','She made a cash withdrawal.','The first is removal of financial support.')]);
P('wither','From Old English witherian, probably related to weather; it means a plant dries and dies, or something weakens or makes someone feel diminished.',[C('wither.s1','枯萎；凋谢','Without rain, the young seedlings began to wither in the hot greenhouse.','沒有雨水，幼苗在炎熱的溫室裡開始枯萎。','plants wither from heat / drought','Verb: of a plant, become dry and die from heat or lack of water.','The seedlings lack water.'),C('wither.s2','衰弱；消亡；使畏缩','Her confidence withered after the manager mocked every proposal she made.','經理嘲笑她提出的每個方案後，她的信心逐漸消退。','confidence / influence withers; wither under a look','Verb: become weaker until almost gone, or make someone feel small.','Repeated mockery diminishes her confidence.')],[M('The seedlings withered during the drought because the soil stayed soaked and their roots received abundant water.','The seedlings withered during the drought because the dry soil deprived them of water.','A plant withers from lack of water, not from being continuously well watered.')],[Q('wither.q1','wither.s1','meaning','Why did the seedlings begin to die?','The hot greenhouse and lack of rain dried them.','Their roots received abundant water.','They were moved to a pond.','Plants wither from heat or lack of water.'),Q('wither.q2','wither.s2','context','What happened to her confidence?','It weakened after repeated mockery.','It grew stronger after praise.','It turned into a greenhouse.','The figurative sense describes something weakening.'),Q('wither.q3','wither.s1','distinction','Which plant is withering?','A dry seedling whose leaves are drooping and dying.','A healthy plant receiving enough water.','A freshly watered plant growing new leaves.','The dry seedling shows the plant sense.'),Q('wither.q4','wither.s2','word-choice','Choose the figurative use.','The project’s influence withered after its funding ended.','The flowers withered in the summer heat.','The plant withered from drought.','The first says influence gradually weakened.')]);
P('withhold','From with- + hold; it means refuse to give something due or keep back information or a feeling.',[C('withhold.s1','拒绝给予；扣留','The landlord may not withhold the tenant’s deposit without a documented reason.','房東不得在沒有書面理由的情況下扣留房客押金。','withhold payment / permission / a deposit','Verb: refuse to give money, permission, or something that is due.','The deposit is due to the tenant.'),C('withhold.s2','隐瞒；忍住不说','The witness chose to withhold one detail until the lawyer could verify it.','證人選擇暫時不透露一個細節，直到律師能查證為止。','withhold information / a comment','Verb: hold back information or a feeling.' ,'The detail is not disclosed yet.')],[M('The landlord withheld the deposit by returning the full amount to the tenant immediately.','The landlord withheld the deposit by refusing to return money due to the tenant.','Withhold means hold back or refuse to give, not return in full.')],[Q('withhold.q1','withhold.s1','meaning','What may the landlord not do without a reason?','Keep the tenant’s due deposit.','Return the full deposit.','Verify a legal document.','Withhold can mean refuse to give something due.'),Q('withhold.q2','withhold.s2','context','Why did the witness keep back one detail?','The lawyer needed to verify it first.','The detail had already been published.','The witness wanted to withdraw money.','Withhold information means not disclose it.'),Q('withhold.q3','withhold.s1','distinction','Which action withholds payment?','An employer refuses to pay wages that are due.','An employer pays wages on time.','An employer gives an extra bonus.','The first holds back money due.'),Q('withhold.q4','withhold.s2','word-choice','Choose the information sense.','The agency withheld the report until the inquiry ended.','The bank withheld cash from an ATM.','The landlord withheld a deposit.','The first delays disclosure of information.')]);
P('within','From with + in; it means inside a place or limits, before a time limit or not beyond a measure, or inside oneself or a group.',[C('within.s1','在……里面；在……范围内','The lost key was somewhere within the locked laboratory.','遺失的鑰匙就在上鎖的實驗室內某處。','within a room / group / boundary','Preposition/adverb: inside a place, group, or area.','The key is inside the lab.'),C('within.s2','在（时间、距离、数量）之内','Please submit the completed form within five working days.','請在五個工作天內提交填妥的表格。','within a time / distance / limit','Preposition: before the end of a period or not beyond a stated amount.','The deadline is no later than five days.'),C('within.s3','在内心；在内部','She found within herself the courage to speak openly at the hearing.','她在自己內心找到勇氣，在聽證會上坦率發言。','find / feel something within oneself','Adverb/preposition: inside, especially in a person’s mind or feelings.','The courage is internal.')],[M('The form was due within five working days, so the clerk waited six months before submitting it.','The form was due within five working days, so the clerk submitted it by the deadline.','Within a stated period means before that period ends.')],[Q('within.q1','within.s1','meaning','Where was the lost key?','Inside the locked laboratory.','Beyond the city limits.','In five working days.','Within can mean inside a place.'),Q('within.q2','within.s2','context','When should the form be submitted?','Before five working days have passed.','After six months.','Only inside the laboratory.','Within a time limit means before it ends.'),Q('within.q3','within.s3','distinction','Where did she find the courage?','Inside her own feelings and mind.','On the roof of the building.','Beyond the deadline.','Within oneself is an inner mental location.'),Q('within.q4','within.s2','word-choice','Choose the time-limit use.','The package will arrive within two days.','The package is within the warehouse.','She found patience within herself.','The first gives a maximum time period.')]);
P('without','From Old English wiþūtan, “outside”; it means not having or using something, not doing an action, or being in a state lacking something just mentioned.',[C('without.s1','没有；缺乏','The hikers continued without a map after the paper guide was lost.','紙本指南遺失後，健行者沒有地圖仍繼續前行。','without money / help / a map','Preposition: not having or not using something.','They lack a map.'),C('without.s2','不；未（做某事）','He left the laboratory without locking the outer door.','他離開實驗室時沒有鎖上外門。','without + -ing','Preposition: not doing the action named by the following verb form.','He did not lock the door.'),C('without.s3','在没有该物的情况下','She could not imagine a morning without coffee after years of the same routine.','多年維持相同作息後，她無法想像早晨沒有咖啡的情況。','live / work / imagine without something','Preposition: in a state of not having the thing just mentioned.','The morning is described as lacking coffee.')],[M('He left without locking the laboratory, meaning he carefully locked both doors before going home.','He left without locking the laboratory, so the outer door remained unlocked.','Without + -ing says the action was not performed.')],[Q('without.q1','without.s1','meaning','What were the hikers missing?','A map.','A locked laboratory.','A cup of coffee.','Without can mean not having something.'),Q('without.q2','without.s2','context','What did he fail to do before leaving?','Lock the outer door.','Find a map.','Drink coffee.','Without locking says the locking action did not happen.'),Q('without.q3','without.s3','distinction','What could she not imagine?','A morning in which she had no coffee.','A morning with extra coffee.','A laboratory door.','The phrase describes a state lacking coffee.'),Q('without.q4','without.s2','grammar','Which sentence uses without followed by an -ing action?','She entered without knocking.','She entered without a key.','She entered with a knock.','Without knocking names an action not performed.')]);
P('without doubt','From without + doubt; it means certainly or with no uncertainty.',[C('without doubt.s1','毫无疑问地；确实地','The restored manuscript is without doubt the most valuable item in the archive.','修復後的手稿無疑是檔案館中最珍貴的藏品。','without doubt, + clause','Adverbial phrase: certainly, leaving no room for uncertainty.','The speaker states certainty.')],[M('Without doubt, the evidence proves the manuscript is genuine, although every expert remains completely uncertain and no test supports it.','Without doubt, the evidence and expert tests establish that the manuscript is genuine.','Without doubt expresses certainty; the contradictory uncertainty in the first sentence makes the phrase incoherent.')],[Q('without doubt.q1','without doubt.s1','meaning','How certain is the speaker about the manuscript?','Completely certain.','Unsure whether it exists.','Certain it is a modern copy.','Without doubt means certainly.'),Q('without doubt.q2','without doubt.s1','context','What is described as most valuable?','The restored manuscript.','A new window.','A damaged cable.','The phrase emphasizes the speaker’s confidence.'),Q('without doubt.q3','without doubt.s1','distinction','Which statement uses without doubt correctly?','Without doubt, the signed record proves her attendance.','Without doubt, nobody can tell whether she attended.','Without doubt means perhaps.','The first expresses a confident conclusion.'),Q('without doubt.q4','without doubt.s1','word-choice','Choose the certainty phrase.','The route is without doubt the safest available.','The route might possibly be safe, but we are unsure.','The route has no physical boundary.','The first means certainly.')]);
P('withstand','From with- + stand, “stand against”; it means endure force or pressure without damage, or resist an attack or difficult test successfully.',[C('withstand.s1','承受住；经受住','The bridge was designed to withstand hurricane-force winds and salt spray.','這座橋的設計能承受颶風級強風與鹽霧。','withstand pressure / heat / force','Verb: not be damaged by force, heat, or pressure.','The structure endures the wind.'),C('withstand.s2','顶住；抵抗成功','The small legal team withstood the company’s challenge and won the appeal.','小型法律團隊頂住公司的挑戰，成功贏得上訴。','withstand an attack / challenge / test','Verb: resist an attack or difficult test successfully.','The team resists the challenge.')],[M('The bridge withstood the storm because the hurricane-force winds tore it apart and sent the deck into the sea.','The bridge withstood the storm and remained intact despite the hurricane-force winds.','Withstand means resist without being defeated or damaged; being torn apart is failure.')],[Q('withstand.q1','withstand.s1','meaning','What was the bridge built to endure?','Hurricane-force wind and salt spray.','A legal appeal.','A spelling test.','This sense concerns surviving physical force.'),Q('withstand.q2','withstand.s2','context','What did the legal team do?','It resisted the company’s challenge and won.','It withdrew from the case immediately.','It built a bridge.','Withstand can mean resist a difficult challenge.'),Q('withstand.q3','withstand.s1','distinction','Which material can withstand high heat?','One that remains undamaged in the heat.','One that melts instantly.','One that avoids a legal hearing.','Withstand means endure without damage.'),Q('withstand.q4','withstand.s2','word-choice','Choose the “resist a test successfully” use.','The small firm withstood the rival’s hostile bid.','The wall withstood the pressure of the flood.','The metal withstood the furnace heat.','The first involves successfully resisting a challenge.')]);
P('witness','From Old English witnes, “knowledge, testimony”; it means someone who sees an event or testifies in court, the act of seeing, or serve as the time/place or evidence of something.',[C('witness.s1','目击者；见证人','A witness saw the delivery van leave the alley just before the alarm sounded.','警報響起前，一名目擊者看見送貨車離開巷子。','an eyewitness / witness to an event','Noun: a person who sees something happen.','The person observes the van.'),C('witness.s2','证人','The witness told the court that she had signed the document in the afternoon.','證人在法庭上表示，她是在下午簽署文件的。','a witness in court; call a witness','Noun: a person who gives evidence in court about what they saw or know.','She gives testimony.'),C('witness.s3','目击；亲眼看见','The entire village witnessed the river rise over the flood markers.','整座村莊都親眼看見河水漫過洪水標記。','witness an event / change','Verb: see something happen, especially something important.','People see the flooding occur.'),C('witness.s4','是……的发生时间；表明','The old station has witnessed a century of arrivals and farewells.','這座老車站見證了一世紀的抵達與離別。','a place / period witnesses events','Verb: be the time or place when something happens, or show that it happened.','The station is the setting over time.')],[M('The witness told the court that she signed the document, but she had never seen it, was absent, and had no information about it.','The witness testified that she saw the document being signed that afternoon.','A court witness gives evidence about what they saw or know; someone with no knowledge cannot support that testimony.')],[Q('witness.q1','witness.s1','meaning','What did the witness observe?','The delivery van leaving the alley.','The court hearing next year.','A metal wire being made.','A witness can be a person who sees an event.'),Q('witness.q2','witness.s2','context','What did the person tell the court?','That she signed the document in the afternoon.','That she never knew what a court was.','That a van entered an alley.','A court witness gives evidence.'),Q('witness.q3','witness.s3','distinction','What did the village witness?','The river rising over the flood markers.','A person giving evidence about a document.','The station’s construction a century ago.','Witness as a verb can mean see an event happen.'),Q('witness.q4','witness.s4','word-choice','Choose the “be the setting or time for” use.','The harbor witnessed the first landing of the expedition.','The sailor witnessed the ship leave.','A witness signed the statement.','The first makes the harbor the place of the event.')]);
P('wits','From wit + plural -s; in this fixed plural, it means the ability to think quickly and intelligently in a difficult situation.',[C('wits.s1','头脑；机智','When the tent collapsed in the storm, the campers kept their wits and moved to the shelter.','暴風雨中帳篷倒塌時，露營者保持冷靜機智，移往避難處。','keep / collect / use one’s wits','Plural noun: the ability to think quickly and intelligently, especially under pressure.','They remain calm and solve the problem.')],[M('The campers kept their wits in the storm by panicking, abandoning the map, and walking toward the flooded river.','The campers kept their wits by staying calm and following the map to shelter.','Keeping one’s wits means thinking clearly under pressure, unlike panicking into danger.')],[Q('wits.q1','wits.s1','meaning','What did the campers keep during the storm?','Their ability to think clearly.','A set of metal wires.','A collection of winter coats.','Keep one’s wits means remain mentally alert.'),Q('wits.q2','wits.s1','context','How did the campers respond when the tent fell?','They stayed calm and moved toward shelter.','They walked into the flooded river.','They forgot where they were.','Their calm decision shows quick thinking.'),Q('wits.q3','wits.s1','distinction','Which person is using their wits?','A driver calmly finds a safe detour after a road closes.','A driver speeds into the closed road without looking.','A driver leaves every map behind.','The first responds intelligently under pressure.'),Q('wits.q4','wits.s1','word-choice','Choose the fixed plural expression.','She kept her wits when the alarm failed.','She kept her witless during the alarm.','She kept one wits on the table.','The standard phrase is “keep one’s wits.”')]);
P('witty','From wit + -y; it describes someone who can make amusing remarks quickly and cleverly.',[C('witty.s1','机智幽默的','The witty host answered the awkward question with a brief, clever joke.','機智的主持人用一句簡短巧妙的笑話回答了尷尬問題。','a witty remark / person / reply','Adjective: able to say amusing things quickly and cleverly.','The host responds with a clever joke.')],[M('The witty host delivered a long, confusing reply that nobody found clever or amusing.','The witty host answered with a short, clever joke that made the guests laugh.','Witty implies clever humor, not a confusing remark that is not amusing.')],[Q('witty.q1','witty.s1','meaning','How did the host answer the awkward question?','With a brief clever joke.','With a long confused silence.','By leaving the room.','Witty describes quick, clever humor.'),Q('witty.q2','witty.s1','context','Which reply is witty?','A quick joke that cleverly answers the question.','A random insult unrelated to the topic.','A long statement no one understands.','The first combines humor and cleverness.'),Q('witty.q3','witty.s1','distinction','What makes a remark witty?','It is amusing and clever.','It is merely loud.','It is always unkind.','Witty remarks use clever humor.'),Q('witty.q4','witty.s1','word-choice','Choose the accurate use.','Her witty reply eased the tension in the room.','Her witty reply confused everyone and had no humor.','The witless response was witty by definition.','The first shows a clever amusing response.')]);
P('wizard','From Middle English wysard, related to wise + -ard; it means a male magician in stories or an exceptionally skilled person.',[C('wizard.s1','男巫；术士','In the fantasy novel, the old wizard guarded the mountain pass with a spell.','奇幻小說中，老術士用咒語守護山隘。','a wizard in a story','Noun: a man believed to have magic powers, especially in stories.','The character uses magic.'),C('wizard.s2','奇才；高手','Ask Priya to repair the spreadsheet; she is a wizard with complicated formulas.','請普莉雅修理試算表吧；她精通複雜公式。','a computer / maths wizard','Noun: a person extremely good at a particular activity or subject.','Priya is highly skilled at formulas.')],[M('The wizard repaired every spreadsheet formula by being unable to use a calculator or understand numbers.','The spreadsheet wizard repaired the formulas quickly because of her exceptional skill.','Wizard can figuratively mean an expert, so inability to understand the task contradicts the use.')],[Q('wizard.q1','wizard.s1','meaning','What protected the mountain pass?','A spell cast by a male magician in the story.','A spreadsheet formula.','A metal cable.','The story sense is a magic-using man.'),Q('wizard.q2','wizard.s2','context','Why ask Priya to repair the spreadsheet?','She is exceptionally skilled with formulas.','She is a magician in a folktale.','She avoids every computer.','Wizard can mean a very skilled person.'),Q('wizard.q3','wizard.s1','distinction','Which character is a story wizard?','A man who uses magic to guard a pass.','An accountant who excels at tax forms.','A student who cannot read.','The first fits the magical story sense.'),Q('wizard.q4','wizard.s2','word-choice','Choose the expert sense.','The network wizard fixed the server in minutes.','The old wizard cast a spell on the mountain.','A spellbook belonged to the wizard.','The first calls someone an expert.')]);
P('woad','From Old English wād, an ancient plant name; it is Isatis tinctoria or the blue dye obtained from its leaves.',[C('woad.s1','菘蓝','The textile conservator identified woad dye on the faded blue cloth.','紡織品修復師在褪色的藍布上辨認出菘藍染料。','woad plant / dye','Noun: Isatis tinctoria, or the blue dye made from its leaves.','The dye derives from the named plant.')],[M('The conservator identified woad dye on the cloth, although the blue color came from a synthetic pigment unrelated to the woad plant.','The conservator found woad, a blue dye traditionally obtained from the plant Isatis tinctoria.','Woad names the plant or its dye, not an unrelated synthetic pigment.')],[Q('woad.q1','woad.s1','meaning','What did the conservator identify?','A traditional blue dye from Isatis tinctoria.','A kind of aircraft wing.','A small glass window.','Woad is the plant or its blue dye.'),Q('woad.q2','woad.s1','context','Where did the dye appear?','On a faded blue textile.','Inside a bank account.','On a metal cable.','The context concerns historic blue cloth dye.'),Q('woad.q3','woad.s1','distinction','Which statement about woad is correct?','Its leaves can provide a blue dye.','It is a telegraph message.','It means to walk away.','Woad is Isatis tinctoria or its dye.'),Q('woad.q4','woad.s1','word-choice','Choose the botanical/dye use.','The museum displayed woad plants beside cloth colored with their dye.','The museum described woad as an electrical wire.','The woad altered the aircraft’s wingspan.','The first connects the plant with its blue dye.')]);
P('wobble','Possibly from Middle English wabbelen, a frequentative of wabben; it means rock unsteadily, a slight rocking movement, or a loss of certainty.',[C('wobble.s1','摇摆','The loose table began to wobble whenever someone leaned on its uneven corner.','只要有人靠在桌子不平的角落，鬆動的桌子就開始搖晃。','wobble from side to side; a wobbling table','Verb/noun: rock unsteadily or a slight unsteady movement.','The table moves unevenly.'),C('wobble.s1','动摇；不确定','After two poor rehearsals, the lead singer’s confidence began to wobble.','兩次排練失常後，主唱的信心開始動搖。','confidence / support wobbles','Verb: become less certain or stable.','The singer becomes unsure.')],[M('The table wobbled on its uneven leg, but stayed perfectly rigid and did not move at all.','The table wobbled on its uneven leg, rocking slightly whenever it was touched.','A wobbling object moves unsteadily, rather than remaining completely still.')],[Q('wobble.q1','wobble.s1','meaning','What did the loose table do?','It rocked unsteadily when touched.','It stayed perfectly fixed.','It transmitted a photograph.','Wobble means move unsteadily.'),Q('wobble.q2','wobble.s1','context','What happened to the singer’s confidence?','It became less certain after poor rehearsals.','It became a piece of furniture.','It increased without limit.','The figurative sense means become unstable or uncertain.'),Q('wobble.q3','wobble.s1','distinction','Which object is wobbling?','A loose sign rocking back and forth in the wind.','A sign firmly bolted to a wall and motionless.','A sign painted blue.','The first moves unsteadily.'),Q('wobble.q4','wobble.s1','word-choice','Choose the uncertainty sense.','Support for the proposal began to wobble after the cost estimate.','The chair wobbled on one short leg.','The table gave a slight wobble.','The first describes support becoming uncertain.')]);
})();



